Subject: [PATCH 001/137] C74 reward: user-facing score surface + read-only
 reward simulation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Validate the reward pipeline with real numbers before any emission wiring.
Both additions are strictly read-only: no emission, no cap changes, no money
moved, no on-chain deploy/mint.

- Migration 20260820200000_c74_reward_simulation.sql:
  * c74_my_contribution() — auth'd user sees their OWN score breakdown
    (gameplay/loyalty/reputation/referrals/vip), tier + multiplier. No promise.
  * admin_c74_reward_simulation(p_limit, p_daily_pool) — full gate pipeline:
    Score -> Eligible -> per-user daily cap -> lifetime cap -> global daily ->
    reserve headroom -> simulated emission, with the binding-gate result.
    Reads caps if present (defaults 100/day, 2000 lifetime); creates/changes
    nothing. Emits nothing.
- IgContribution.tsx (/ig/contribution, AuthGuard) — user-facing score surface
  in the .ig system with a not-guaranteed contract; linked from IgRewards.
- AdminC74Contribution: 'Reward simulation' section (pool input, gate chips,
  reserve-gate result, per-user pipeline table).
- docs/C74-CONTRIBUTION-SCORE-DESIGN.md: Phase 1.5 pipeline + live validation.

Validated read-only on live data: 95 eligible, raw-after-caps 8543 C74, reserve
headroom 1115.56, earn_enabled=false -> simulated emission 0.00 (gate:
earn_disabled). The gates demonstrably bind.

