@@ -0,0 +1,158 @@
+# Telegram Human Play + Bot Economy — design-first, money-safe
+
+**Status:** DESIGN + read-only simulation only. **Nothing is deployed, migrated,
+minted, paid out, or enabled.** No real-money withdrawal, no flag change, no
+wallet transfer. Build/enable happens only after explicit approval, in stages.
+
+Core idea: people play **for free** (no deposits). The platform first earns
+**real external revenue** (sponsorships, ads, affiliate, optional premium). Only a
+capped slice of that **verified** revenue funds a reward pool, and rewards are paid
+**from the pool only**, with full provenance. Sustainable, and never funded by user
+deposits, minting, or phantom balances.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Architecture / design
+
+```
+Telegram User ──▶ Free Human/Bot Gameplay ──▶ Engagement
+                                                   │
+        External monetization (NOT user money):    │
+        sponsorship · advertising · affiliate ·     │
+        optional premium                            ▼
+                          ┌───────────── Verified Revenue Pool ─────────────┐
+                          │  only booked, verified external revenue counts   │
+                          └───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────┘
+                                                   │ allocation_pct (e.g. 40%)
+                                                   ▼
+                                        Reward Pool (allocated)
+                                                   │ engagement share, capped
+                                                   ▼
+                                        User Reward (C74 reward units)
+                                                   │ (later, separate, gated)
+                                                   ▼
+                                        Redemption — reserve-invariant gated, OFF now
+```
+
+**Hard separation (three independent ledgers):**
+
+| Ledger | Holds | Never touches |
+|---|---|---|
+| **Casino user balances** (`casino_wallets`) | real-money user liability | reward pool, C74 reserve |
+| **C74 backing reserve** (`c74_reserve_ledger`) | operator-funded USDT backing | this economy's revenue/pool |
+| **Human-Play revenue + reward pool** (NEW, design) | external revenue → pool → grants | user deposits, minting |
+
+The Human-Play economy is **its own ledger**. It reads none of, and writes none
+of, `casino_wallets` or `c74_reserve_ledger`.
+
+## 2. Revenue → reward accounting flow
+
+Proposed tables (DESIGN — **not created** in this PR):
+
+- `humanplay_revenue(id, source ∈ {sponsorship,advertising,affiliate,premium},
+  amount_usd, external_ref, verified_by, verified_at, note, created_at)`
+  — append-only; a row counts only when `verified_at` is set (dual-control:
+  booked by one admin, verified by another, like reserve contributions).
+- `humanplay_reward_pool(id, period, allocated_units, source_revenue_usd,
+  allocation_pct, created_by, created_at)` — the pool allocated for a period.
+- `humanplay_reward_grants(id, pool_id, user_id, units, engagement_share,
+  revenue_provenance jsonb, status, created_at)` — one row per user reward, each
+  carrying its provenance (which revenue → which pool → this user).
+
+Money-safe accounting rules:
+
+1. `allocated_units ≤ allocation_pct × Σ(verified revenue)` — never allocate from
+   unverified or future revenue.
+2. `Σ(grants.units for pool) ≤ pool.allocated_units` — never distribute more than
+   the pool holds.
+3. Each grant stores `revenue_provenance` = {sources, pool_id, engagement_share}.
+4. Rewards are **reward units (C74)**, not cash. Converting C74 → USDT stays behind
+   the existing reserve invariant and is **OFF**.
+
+## 3. Telegram bot / user flow
+
+1. User opens the bot (`/start`) — no deposit, no wallet required.
+2. Free gameplay: solo, vs-bot, or human-vs-human mini-games. Bots are **house/AI
+   opponents** for fun, or **verified bot partners**; unverified automation is
+   excluded from rewards.
+3. Engagement accrues from *genuine* signals (rounds played, streaks, missions,
+   referrals of real humans) — the same philosophy as the Contribution Score.
+4. Monetization runs **around** the gameplay: sponsor placements, ads, affiliate
+   links, optional premium cosmetics/features. This is the only money in.
+5. Rewards are granted from the pool per §2, capped per §4, shown to the user as
+   "reward units earned — subject to availability", **never** "guaranteed $X".
+6. Redemption is a **later, separate, gated** step (reserve-invariant, KYC, OFF now).
+
+## 4. Reward-pool invariant
+
+```
+I1  pool_allocated      ≤ allocation_pct × verified_revenue     (no over-allocation)
+I2  Σ distributed_units ≤ pool_allocated                        (no over-distribution)
+I3  every grant has provenance: revenue_source → pool → user
+I4  inputs are external revenue ONLY — never user deposits, never minting
+I5  per-user DAILY and LIFETIME caps enforced; bots/flagged/quarantined get 0
+I6  remaining_pool = pool_allocated − distributed ≥ 0 at all times
+```
+
+If verified revenue = 0 → pool = 0 → **no rewards** (exactly like the casino side:
+no reserve → no redemption). The economy can only grow with real revenue.
+
+## 5. Admin reporting / simulation
+
+- **Read-only simulator (this PR):** `scripts/humanplay-economy-simulator.py` —
+  offline, no DB. Given hypothetical revenue + engagement, it computes pool,
+  per-user distribution (capped), remaining, and asserts I1–I6.
+  Demo run ($1,000 verified, 40% allocation, 7 users):
+
+  | | value |
+  |---|---:|
+  | Verified revenue | $1,000.00 (sponsor 500 · ads 250 · affiliate 180 · premium 70) |
+  | Reward pool (40%) | 400.00 C74 |
+  | Eligible / excluded | 4 / 3 (bot, fraud-flag, quarantined excluded) |
+  | Distributed | 194.44 C74 |
+  | Remaining pool | 205.56 C74 |
+  | Caps | daily 100 · lifetime 2000 — bob capped to 40 (daily headroom), carol to 10 (lifetime headroom) |
+  | Invariants | **all PASS** |
+
+- **Admin view (NEXT step, after approval — not built here):** "Human Play Revenue
+  / Reward Pool" showing verified revenue by source, allocated pool, distributed
+  rewards, remaining pool, and the invariant status — mirroring the existing
+  Operator-Profit / Contribution tabs, read-only.
+
+## 6. Abuse / fraud protections
+
+- **Bot vs human:** house/AI bots and unverified automation are **excluded** from
+  rewards; only humans and *verified* bot partners earn. Turing/behaviour checks,
+  device + IP fingerprinting, velocity limits.
+- **Sybil / multi-account:** referrals count only verified humans; per-device and
+  per-IP caps; KYC gate for higher reward tiers; shared-payout-destination
+  detection (reuses the payout-destination registry concept).
+- **Engagement gaming:** rewards scale with *validated* engagement, not raw taps;
+  anomaly detection (impossibly fast rounds, scripted patterns) flags accounts.
+- **Caps:** per-user daily + lifetime caps and a global pool ceiling bound blast
+  radius; flagged/quarantined accounts get 0.
+- **Provenance audit:** every grant is traceable to a verified revenue row; unfunded
+  grants are impossible by construction (I2).
+
+## 7. Separation from user liabilities + C74 reserve
+
+- Human-Play revenue/pool/grants live in their **own tables**; the accounting never
+  reads or writes `casino_wallets` (user liability) or `c74_reserve_ledger`.
+- Reward units are **C74**, but they are **granted from the reward pool**, not
+  minted and not drawn from the reserve. The reserve backs **redemption** only, and
+  redemption stays invariant-gated and OFF.
+- No user deposit ever funds a reward (I4). No unbacked win becomes USDT. No phantom
+  balance is converted. No guaranteed-profit promise is made anywhere.
+
+---
+
+## What this PR contains / what it does NOT
+
+**Contains:** this design doc + the offline read-only simulator (`--selftest`
+passing). **Does NOT:** create any table, RPC, edge function, admin UI, flag, or
+Telegram integration; move no money; mint nothing; change no cap.
+
+**Stop point (per instruction):** design + read-only simulation delivered, numbers
+reported. Nothing is deployed or enabled. The next stage (revenue ledger + dual-
+control verification + admin view + Telegram wiring, all still money-OFF) proceeds
+**only on explicit approval**.
