+# Payment-collection → recipient-settlement — design-first, money-safe
+
+**Status:** DESIGN + read-only simulation only. **Nothing is deployed, migrated,
+integrated with a provider, or enabled.** No provider keys, no nodal account, no
+money movement.
+
+Use case: a customer pays (through Telegram, without needing their own card/UPI on
+our side), and a **verified recipient** receives a settlement — while the platform
+keeps only its **fee** as revenue. This is a **marketplace / split-settlement**
+model on top of a **licensed** payment aggregator.
+
+## What this explicitly is NOT
+
+It does **not** copy the personal **"Gift to relatives" IMPS narration** pattern.
+Dressing business collections as personal gifts misrepresents the transaction and
+breaches bank/PSP terms and AML/tax rules. Rejected by design.
+
+## 1. Architecture
+
+```
+Customer payment  (Telegram entry point; hosted checkout / provider link)
+   ↓   funds settle into the LICENSED PA's NODAL / ESCROW account — never the operator's own account
+Licensed Payment Aggregator (RBI PA) / approved collection rail
+   ↓
+Platform reconciliation ledger  (per-payment: provider_txn_id · recipient_id · status)
+   ├─ Platform FEE            → verified platform revenue     (operator's)
+   └─ Recipient amount        → SETTLEMENT LIABILITY           (pass-through, owed out)
+   ↓   only to a KYC-verified recipient, via the provider's route/split product
+Settlement to recipient
+```
+
+## 2. Revenue → settlement accounting
+
+Proposed tables (DESIGN — **not created** here):
+
+- `settlement_payments(id, provider_txn_id, amount_collected, fee, recipient_amount,
+  recipient_id, status ∈ {collected,settled,held,blocked,refunded}, collected_at,
+  settled_at, reconciled_at)` — one row per customer payment; `provider_txn_id` and
+  `recipient_id` are **mandatory** to process.
+- `settlement_recipients(id, kyc_status, payout_method, verified_by, verified_at)` —
+  KYC-verified recipients only (dual-control verification, like the payout-
+  destination registry).
+- Fee → **`treasury_ledger`** as `kind='settlement_fee'` (verified revenue). The
+  recipient amount is a **liability**, never revenue.
+
+## 3. The four-ledger separation (hard)
+
+| Ledger | Holds | Never funds |
+|---|---|---|
+| Casino user balances | real-money user liability | — |
+| C74 backing reserve | operator USDT backing C74 | settlements |
+| Operator profit | swept surplus / fees | settlements |
+| **Settlement liability** (NEW) | customer→recipient pass-through | operator profit / reserve / user funds |
+
+Customer principal is **never** platform revenue; only the fee is. The recipient
+amount is held in the provider's nodal/escrow and settled out — it never becomes
+operator money.
+
+## 4. Settlement invariant
+
+```
+S1  fee + recipient_amount == amount_collected            (per payment; no leakage)
+S2  Σ settled ≤ Σ collected − Σ fees                      (never settle beyond net collected)
+S3  platform_revenue == Σ fees ONLY                       (principal is never revenue)
+S4  settle ONLY to KYC-verified recipients                (else HELD)
+S5  a settlement is funded ONLY by its matching collected payment
+    (never from operator profit / C74 reserve / user funds)
+S6  every payment carries provider_txn_id + recipient_id + status  (else BLOCKED)
+```
+
+## 5. Admin reporting / simulation
+
+- **Read-only simulator (this PR):** `scripts/settlement-simulator.py` — offline, no
+  DB, no keys. Splits collected payments into fee vs recipient liability, gates
+  settlement on verification + provenance, and asserts S1–S6.
+  Demo run (6 payments, 3% + flat 2 fee):
+
+  | | value |
+  |---|---:|
+  | Total collected (customer money) | 4,000.00 |
+  | Platform revenue (**fees only**) | **132.00** |
+  | Recipient liability (pass-through) | 3,868.00 |
+  | Settled to verified recipients | 1,451.00 |
+  | Held (unverified / not-ready) | 966.00 |
+  | Blocked (missing provider txn / recipient id) | 1,451.00 |
+  | Outstanding liability | 2,417.00 |
+  | Invariants S1–S6 | **all PASS** |
+
+- **Admin view (NEXT step, after approval — not built here):** "Collections &
+  Settlements" — collected, fees (revenue), recipient liability, settled, held,
+  blocked, outstanding, and reconciliation status, read-only.
+
+## 6. Abuse / fraud + compliance protections
+
+- **KYC on both sides:** payer per PA norms; **recipient must be KYC-verified**
+  before any settlement.
+- **AML:** transaction monitoring, velocity/threshold limits, sanction/PEP screening
+  via the provider; **truthful narration** (no gift/personal disguise).
+- **Provenance-or-block:** a payment with no `provider_txn_id` or `recipient_id` is
+  **blocked**, never settled (S6).
+- **Reconciliation:** every payment matched to the provider's settlement report
+  before `settled`; mismatches quarantined.
+- **No commingling:** recipient funds stay in the provider nodal/escrow; operator
+  touches only the fee.
+
+## 7. The hard external gate (cannot be self-certified)
+
+Collecting money and settling to third parties = acting as a **payment
+intermediary**. This requires an **RBI Payment Aggregator licence**, or building on
+a **licensed PA/PSP's route / split-settlement product** with a **nodal/escrow**
+account and their KYC/AML. This is a **legal/licensing dependency** — external, not
+solvable in code. The architecture above is valid **only** on top of that licensed
+rail. No provider is integrated and no funds move in this PR.
+
+---
+
+## What this PR contains / does NOT
+
+**Contains:** this design doc + the offline read-only simulator (`--selftest`
+passing). **Does NOT:** create any table/RPC/edge-function/admin-UI, integrate any
+provider, hold any keys, or move any money.
+
+**Stop point (per instruction):** design + read-only simulation delivered, numbers
+reported. The next stage (reconciliation ledger + recipient registry + provider
+integration + admin view, all still money-OFF) proceeds **only on explicit
+approval**, and only on a licensed rail.
