+## Typed client
+
+The Supabase clients are generic over the generated `Database` types
+(`utils/supabase/database.types.ts`), so `.from(...)`, `.select(...)`, inserts and
+RPC calls are fully typed:
+
+```ts
+import type { Tables, TablesInsert, Enums } from "@/utils/supabase/database.types";
+type Wallet = Tables<"casino_wallets">;
+// const { data } = await supabase.from("casino_wallets").select("*"); // data: Wallet[] | null
+```
+
+`database.types.ts` is a copy of the root app's `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts`
+(same schema). Regenerate after a schema change with:
+
+```bash
+npx supabase gen types typescript --project-id smcwrriaraptzjhqdktg > utils/supabase/database.types.ts
+```
+
 ## Notes
 
 - Env keys are **public** (publishable/anon) — safe in the client bundle. Never put
