+# Real-money flow — Payment → Ledger → IG Wallet → Withdrawal (design-first, money-safe)
+
+**Status:** DESIGN + read-only simulation only. **Nothing is deployed, migrated,
+integrated with a payment provider, or enabled.** No provider keys, no live rail,
+no money movement. `real_money_enabled` stays **OFF**.
+
+Builds on the existing money-safe work: the **settlement** design
+(`PAYMENT-COLLECTION-SETTLEMENT-ARCHITECTURE.md`), the **operator-profit** dual-control
+ledger, the **C74 reserve invariant**, and the **Razorpay webhook** trust model.
+
+## The two HARD prerequisites (external — cannot be coded around)
+1. **License + PSP approval** — real-money gaming deposits (card/UPI) require a
+   proper gaming/gambling licence *and* payment-processor approval for that merchant
+   category. Stripe/Razorpay prohibit unlicensed gambling. Not self-certifiable.
+2. **Operator treasury funding** — the operational treasury must hold real assets ≥
+   user liabilities (solvency). Latest reading: **$0** → real-money launch is blocked
+   until funded with legitimate operator capital.
+
+Neither DNS nor code unblocks these. Until both are met **and** you explicitly flip
+the flag, `real_money_enabled = false`.
+
+## 1. End-to-end flow
+
+```
+Customer real payment (licensed PSP: card/UPI)
+   ↓  funds → provider settlement/nodal account (never the operator's own account)
+VERIFIED provider webhook  (HMAC signature + idempotency, credit the authoritative
+   amount only — same trust model as razorpay-webhook)
+   ↓
+IMMUTABLE LEDGER  (append-only; every entry carries provenance)
+   ↓  deposit entry
+IG WALLET credit  (user liability; balance is DERIVED from the ledger, never mutated directly)
+   ↓
+Play → IG game settlement (bet/win) → ledger entries (game_round provenance) → balance
+   ↓
+Withdrawal request → KYC + eligibility (wagering gate) + verified destination
+   → ledger debit → payout rail (verified wallet/bank)  → reconciliation
+```
+
+## 2. Four-ledger separation (unchanged, hard)
+
+| Ledger | Holds | Never funds |
+|---|---|---|
+| **User wallet** (IG balances) | real-money user liability | operator profit, reserve |
+| **C74 reserve** | operator USDT backing C74 | user withdrawals |
+| **Operator revenue** | fees / GGR surplus | user liabilities |
+| **Settlement liability** | customer→recipient pass-through | anything else |
+
+## 3. Invariants (money-safe — asserted in the simulator)
+
+```
+L1  every balance change is an APPEND-ONLY ledger entry with provenance
+    (provider_txn_id / game_round / withdrawal_id)
+L2  a deposit credits the wallet ONLY on a verified provider settlement
+    (bad signature / no provider_txn_id → rejected, no credit)
+L3  wallet balance == Σ(ledger deltas for that user)   (ledger is the source of truth;
+    balances are derived, never directly written)
+L4  a withdrawal executes ONLY if: KYC-approved AND destination verified AND
+    amount ≤ balance AND wagering-gate passed (wagered ≥ deposited) AND amount > 0
+L5  SOLVENCY: Σ user liabilities ≤ real assets held (treasury). If assets < liabilities,
+    real-money withdrawals are BLOCKED (this is the treasury-funding gate)
+L6  no credit without a real inbound settlement; no unbacked win → real money; no phantom
+L7  real_money_enabled = false → nothing executes; the payout rail is never called
+```
+
+## 4. Read-only simulation (this PR)
+
+`scripts/realmoney-flow-simulator.py` — offline, no DB / keys / money. Processes
+deposits / plays / withdrawals through the ledger, derives balances, and asserts
+L1–L7. `--selftest` passes.
+
+Demo run (flag **OFF** — default):
+
+| | value |
+|---|---:|
+| deposits credited | 150.00 (1 rejected — unverified, no provider_txn_id) |
+| user liabilities | 110.00 (solvent vs 1000 treasury) |
+| withdrawals executed | **0** (flag off) |
+| withdrawals blocked | 3 — reasons: `real_money_disabled(flag_off)`, `wagering_gate_not_met`, `kyc_not_approved` |
+| invariants L1–L7 | **all PASS** |
+
+Preview run (`--enabled`, still no real money — shows what *would* happen): only the
+one eligible withdrawal (alice, KYC ✓, wagered ≥ deposited ✓, ≤ balance) would
+execute; bob (wagering gate) and alice-W3 (KYC) stay blocked. Invariants still hold.
+
+## 5. Proposed schema (DESIGN — not created here)
+
+- `ledger_entries(id, user_id, delta, kind ∈ {deposit,bet,win,withdrawal,fee,adjustment},
+  provenance jsonb, created_at)` — append-only; **no updates/deletes**; balance is a view
+  `Σ delta`.
+- Deposits reuse the verified-webhook credit path (signature + idempotency).
+- Withdrawals reuse `rpc_compute_withdrawable` (wagering gate) + a **verified
+  destination registry** (KYC'd, dual-control) + the reserve/solvency check.
+- `platform_settings.real_money_enabled` (default **false**) gates the entire path.
+
+## 6. Admin (NEXT step, after approval — not built here)
+
+Read-only "Real-money Ops" view: ledger tail, per-user derived balances, solvency
+(liabilities vs treasury), withdrawal queue with the gate reasons, reconciliation
+status. No money controls until the prerequisites are met.
+
+---
+
+## What this PR contains / does NOT
+
+**Contains:** this design doc + the offline read-only simulator (`--selftest` passing).
+**Does NOT:** create any table/RPC/edge-function/admin-UI, integrate any PSP, hold any
+keys, enable any flag, or move any money.
+
+**Stop point (per instruction):** design + read-only simulation delivered, numbers
+reported. Real payment keys, real deposits, withdrawals, and emission/payout stay
+**disabled** until (1) license + PSP approval, (2) treasury funding, and (3) your
+explicit go-ahead — then a small supervised live test → reconciliation → scale.
