+# Reconciliation — PSP settlement ↔ internal ledger ↔ bank/on-chain (design-first, money-safe)
+
+**Status:** DESIGN + read-only simulation only. **Nothing is deployed, integrated with
+a payment provider, or enabled.** No provider keys, no live rail, no money movement.
+This is the missing piece flagged in `REAL-MONEY-LAUNCH-READINESS.md` §5 and go-live
+step 4 — the daily three-way tie-out that must be **green in sandbox before** any
+real-money withdrawal is enabled, and run **daily** thereafter.
+
+Builds directly on the real-money ledger design
+(`REAL-MONEY-PAYMENT-LEDGER-WALLET-WITHDRAWAL.md`) — reconciliation is the control that
+*proves* invariant **L5 (solvency)** and **L2 (verified-deposit-only)** hold in reality,
+not just in the code path.
+
+## Why reconciliation is a hard gate (not optional bookkeeping)
+
+Three independent systems each record the same money:
+
+1. **PSP settlement report** — what the processor says it settled to us (per
+   `provider_txn_id`: gross, fee, net, status).
+2. **Internal ledger** — the deposit credits we booked to user wallets.
+3. **Bank / on-chain movement** — cash we can actually observe arriving.
+
+If these three ever disagree, **either users are over-credited (we owe money we never
+received) or under-credited (we're holding money we haven't booked).** The first breaks
+solvency; the second is a customer-funds problem. The only safe posture is: **a credit
+is final only once all three agree.** Everything else is an exception that a human works,
+under dual control — never auto-corrected by code.
+
+## 1. The three-way tie-out
+
+```
+PSP settlement line (settled, provider_txn_id, net)
+        │  must match 1:1
+        ▼
+Internal ledger deposit credit (provider_txn_id, amount)      amount == PSP.net
+        │  must match 1:1
+        ▼
+Bank / on-chain movement (provider_txn_id, net)               net == PSP.net
+```
+
+A row is **CLEAN** only when all three legs are present and agree within tolerance
+(1 cent). Anything else is one of the exception classes below.
+
+## 2. Invariants (money-safe — asserted in the simulator)
+
+```
+R1  1:1 — every CLEAN internal deposit credit maps to exactly one *settled* PSP line
+    with the same provider_txn_id.  No credit is "clean" without a settlement line.
+R2  amount agreement — CLEAN match requires PSP.net == ledger.amount (±1c). Any
+    divergence is a MISMATCH exception; never silently accepted or auto-corrected.
+R3  no orphan credit — a ledger credit with no PSP line is QUARANTINED (must not be
+    treated as real money). Reported, never deleted.
+R4  no dropped settlement — a settled PSP line with no ledger credit is a MISSING_CREDIT
+    exception (money arrived we haven't booked). Reported for manual booking; the
+    reconciler never auto-credits.
+R5  idempotency — a provider_txn_id appearing more than once in the ledger is a
+    DUPLICATE breach (double credit). Every copy is flagged.
+R6  three-way settle — a CLEAN row requires PSP.net == ledger.amount == bank.net. A leg
+    that disagrees (e.g. PSP settled but bank shows nothing) is a BANK_MISMATCH exception.
+R7  read-only — the reconciler mutates nothing: no credit, debit, correction, or delete.
+    It returns a classification + totals only. Booking / quarantine / write-off are a
+    separate, dual-control, human action.
+```
+
+## 3. Exception classes (what a human works, under dual control)
+
+| Class | Meaning | Safe action (dual-control) |
+|---|---|---|
+| `amount_mismatch` | PSP.net ≠ ledger.amount | Investigate; correct the *wrong* side by adjusting-entry (never edit history) |
+| `orphan_credit` | ledger credit, no PSP line | **Quarantine** — do not treat as real; reverse if unbacked |
+| `missing_credit` | settled PSP, no ledger | Book the credit manually after verifying the settlement line |
+| `duplicate_credit` | provider_txn_id booked twice | Reverse the extra copy (idempotency breach) |
+| `bank_mismatch` | PSP settled but bank/on-chain disagrees | Hold; chase the PSP; do not release withdrawals against it |
+| `non_settled_psp_backed` | credit backed by a pending/failed/refunded line | Reverse or hold until the line actually settles |
+
+**None of these are auto-remediated.** The reconciler classifies; a person acts.
+
+## 4. Read-only simulation (this PR)
+
+`scripts/reconciliation-simulator.py` — offline, no DB / keys / money. Feeds three
+record sets (PSP / ledger / bank) through the matcher and asserts R1–R7. `--selftest`
+passes.
+
+Demo run (a deliberately messy book):
+
+| | value |
+|---|---:|
+| PSP settled total | 525.00 |
+| ledger total | 515.00 |
+| bank/on-chain total | 350.00 |
+| three-way totals agree | **False** (exceptions present) |
+| CLEAN matched | 2 rows, 150.00 |
+| exceptions | 6 — `amount_mismatch`, `orphan_credit`, `missing_credit`, `duplicate_credit`×2, `bank_mismatch` |
+| `reconciled_clean` (advisory) | **False** |
+| invariants R1–R7 | **all PASS** |
+
+A fully-clean book (`--selftest`'s second case) reconciles: `reconciled_clean=True`,
+`three_way_totals_agree=True`, zero exceptions.
+
+## 5. Proposed schema + job (DESIGN — not created here)
+
+- `psp_settlement_lines(provider_txn_id PK, gross, fee, net, status, report_date, raw jsonb)`
+  — ingested from the PSP's settlement report (read-only mirror; never the source of a
+  credit on its own).
+- Reconcile against `ledger_entries` (kind=`deposit`, provenance→provider_txn_id) and a
+  `bank_movements` / on-chain-observation table.
+- `reconciliation_runs(id, run_date, clean_count, exception_count, totals jsonb)` +
+  `reconciliation_exceptions(run_id, class, provider_txn_id, detail jsonb, resolved_by,
+  resolved_at)` — an **append-only** audit trail; resolving an exception writes a new
+  adjusting entry, it never edits ledger history.
+- A scheduled daily job produces the run; **withdrawals stay gated on the latest run
+  being clean** (ties into L5 solvency + go-live step 4).
+
+## 6. Admin (NEXT step, after approval — not built here)
+
+Read-only "Reconciliation" view: latest run status (clean / N exceptions), the exception
+worklist grouped by class, three-way totals, and history. Resolving an exception is a
+dual-control action (propose → approve) that writes an adjusting entry — no direct edits.
+
+---
+
+## What this PR contains / does NOT
+
+**Contains:** this design doc + the offline read-only simulator (`--selftest` passing).
+**Does NOT:** create any table/RPC/edge-function/admin-UI/scheduled-job, ingest any real
+PSP report, integrate any PSP, hold any keys, enable any flag, or move any money.
+
+**Stop point (per instruction):** design + read-only simulation delivered, numbers
+reported. This closes the reconciliation gap in the launch-readiness doc (§5 / go-live
+step 4). Real payment keys, deposits, withdrawals, and emission/payout stay **disabled**
+until license + PSP approval + treasury funding + your explicit go-ahead — then
+reconciliation must be **green in sandbox** before the first supervised withdrawal.
