@@ -0,0 +1,157 @@
+# Unified Real-Money Master Gate — Design
+
+**Status:** DESIGN / REVIEW ONLY — nothing in this document is applied.
+**Depends on:** `docs/REAL-MONEY-READINESS-AUDIT.md` (findings)
+**UI baseline:** tag `ui-freeze-toptier-v1` → `d0e80ed` (unchanged)
+**Constraint:** no production behavior change here; no SQL run against the DB; no
+flags flipped; no keys touched; no money moved. All SQL/code below is a proposal
+to be reviewed and applied later under a change window with a rollback plan.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Problem this solves
+
+The audit found a **split state**: automated payout + C74 emission are gated OFF,
+but the inbound side (`mode=live`, live Razorpay, `evm/btc/ton_deposits_enabled`)
+is configured live — and there is **no single `real_money_enabled` key** at all.
+"Real money" is currently governed by a scattered set of flags that can drift
+independently, so no one switch can guarantee "all OFF."
+
+**Goal:** one authoritative, fail-closed master gate that governs **both**
+directions (money in *and* money out), with the existing per-rail flags kept as
+secondary defense-in-depth controls.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Design principles
+
+1. **Single source of truth** — one key, `platform_settings.real_money_enabled`.
+2. **Fail-closed** — absent/unknown/malformed value ⇒ treated as `false` (OFF).
+   (This matches today's payout gate, which already does
+   `coalesce((select value='true' … ),false)`.)
+3. **Governs both directions** — inbound (deposit credit, mode routing, PSP) and
+   outbound (withdrawal/payout execution, emission/swap) all read it.
+4. **Defense in depth** — the master gate does **not** replace the per-rail
+   flags; both must permit an action. Master OFF ⇒ everything blocked regardless
+   of per-rail flags. Master ON ⇒ each rail still honors its own flag
+   (`auto_payout_enabled`, gateway `enabled`, `mode`, `c74_phase2_enabled`, …).
+5. **Auditable + dual-control** — every flip writes `audit_logs`; enabling
+   requires a recorded prerequisite checklist and two-person approval.
+6. **Instant kill switch** — flipping to `false` immediately blocks all
+   real-money movement at the next check (no deploy required).
+
+---
+
+## 3. Gate semantics
+
+| Path | `real_money_enabled = false` (default) | `real_money_enabled = true` |
+|---|---|---|
+| Deposit credit (PSP webhook, on-chain crediting) | **blocked / demo-only** | allowed **iff** that rail's own flag is on |
+| `mode` routing (`/deposit` vs demo) | forced demo path | live path honored if `mode=live` |
+| PSP (Razorpay) charge/settle | disabled | honored iff `gateway.enabled && mode=live` |
+| Withdrawal / payout execution | **blocked** (already OFF today) | allowed iff `auto_payout_enabled` (+ L4 gate PASS) |
+| C74 emission / swap payout | **blocked** | allowed iff `c74_phase2_enabled` / `c74_swap_settings.enabled` |
+| Read-only admin/reporting/reconciliation | always allowed | always allowed |
+
+Reconciliation, reporting, and the read-only admin surfaces are **never** gated —
+they must keep working while real money is OFF.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Enforcement points (where the check goes)
+
+The gate is only as good as its call sites. Proposed single choke-points:
+
+- **DB helper (authoritative):** `public.is_real_money_enabled()` — one
+  `SECURITY DEFINER`, `STABLE` function reading the key fail-closed. Every
+  server-side money path calls it; no path reads the raw key directly.
+- **Inbound:**
+  - PSP settlement / webhook crediting handler → refuse to credit when OFF.
+  - On-chain deposit crediting (deposit scanner / `incoming_deposits` →
+    `casino_wallets`) → refuse to credit when OFF.
+  - `mode` routing in the client is a UX hint only; the **authoritative** block
+    is server-side crediting, not the redirect.
+- **Outbound:**
+  - Withdrawal / crypto-payout executor edge function → already checks
+    `real_money_enabled` (via `coalesce`); keep, and ensure it uses the helper.
+  - C74 emission / swap execution → add the same check.
+- **Client (advisory only):** show a "real money OFF" banner on money screens
+  when the gate is off; never rely on the client for enforcement.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Enable procedure (when the day comes — not now)
+
+Enabling is a **governed operation**, not a config edit:
+
+1. Prerequisite checklist recorded (all must be ✅): **license**, **PSP formal
+   approval**, **funded & segregated treasury**, **compliance sign-off**,
+   reconciliation green (0 critical), drift explained.
+2. **Two-person approval** (dual-control) captured in `audit_logs`.
+3. Flip `real_money_enabled=true` in a supervised window.
+4. Per-rail flags enabled deliberately, one at a time, each observed.
+5. Rollback = flip back to `false` (instant kill switch).
+
+---
+
+## 6. Proposed implementation — FOR REVIEW, NOT APPLIED
+
+> None of the following is executed by this document. It is the shape of the
+> change to review. Finalize exact statements, policies, and rollback at review
+> time.
+
+**6a. Fail-closed helper (DB):**
+```sql
+-- REVIEW ONLY
+create or replace function public.is_real_money_enabled()
+returns boolean language sql stable security definer set search_path=public as $$
+  select coalesce((select value = 'true' from platform_settings
+                   where key = 'real_money_enabled'), false);
+$$;
+```
+
+**6b. Seed the key OFF (idempotent):**
+```sql
+-- REVIEW ONLY
+insert into platform_settings(key, value)
+values ('real_money_enabled', 'false')
+on conflict (key) do nothing;   -- never force to true
+```
+
+**6c. Enforcement (illustrative), inbound crediting:**
+```
+-- REVIEW ONLY (pseudocode inside the credit path)
+if not is_real_money_enabled() then
+  reject('real money disabled');   -- do not credit casino_wallets
+end if;
+```
+
+**6d. Controlled inbound-OFF change-set** — carried over from the audit doc §5,
+still **review-only**: `mode → demo`, Razorpay `enabled=false`,
+`evm/btc/ton_deposits_enabled=false`, plus seeding the master key OFF (6b).
+Payout-side gates are already OFF and are left untouched.
+
+---
+
+## 7. Rollout order
+
+1. **This design** → review & approve. *(current step)*
+2. Prepare + review the **controlled inbound-OFF change-set** (audit §5 / 6d).
+3. Apply inbound-OFF in a change window (operator action, not automated here).
+4. Implement the **helper + enforcement** (6a/6c) and wire all money paths through it.
+5. Verify in **demo mode** (deposits blocked, reconciliation still green, read-only surfaces intact).
+6. Only after **license + PSP + funded treasury + compliance** → supervised enable (§5).
+
+---
+
+## 8. Non-goals (explicitly out of scope now)
+
+- Not flipping any flag, not disabling any live rail, not running any SQL against
+  production in this document.
+- Not enabling real money. `real_money_enabled` remains absent/OFF.
+- Not changing the frozen UI baseline (`d0e80ed`).
+
+**Bottom line:** this converts the scattered, drift-prone flag set into one
+fail-closed master gate governing both directions, with a governed enable
+procedure and an instant kill switch — designed now, applied later only under
+review and only after the external gates are met.
-- 
2.43.0


