+# Master Gate — Exact Affected Code Paths
+
+**Status:** DESIGN / REVIEW ONLY — nothing here is applied. No production
+behavior changed; no SQL run; no edge function deployed.
+**Companion to:** `docs/REAL-MONEY-MASTER-GATE-DESIGN.md`
+**Method:** read-only repo sweep (grep + file reads) of `supabase/functions` and `src`.
+
+---
+
+## 0. Critical finding that shapes the wiring
+
+**No money-moving path currently reads `real_money_enabled`.** A repo-wide search
+found the key only in the **read-only audit/reporting** surfaces
+(`admin_real_money_ops_overview`, `admin_withdrawal_gate_eval`,
+`AdminRealMoneyOps.tsx`, `AdminWithdrawalGate.tsx`). The actual executors gate on
+**`auto_payout_enabled`** (payouts) and **per-rail flags** (deposits). So today
+`real_money_enabled` is a *label*, enforced by nothing.
+
+➡️ The master gate must be **wired into the executors and credit paths**, not
+just reported. The list below is where.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Outbound — payout / on-chain send
+
+| Path | File · line | Current gate | Add |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Operator payout executor (TRC20) | `supabase/functions/operator-payout-execute/index.ts:137` | `if (!enabled) …` where `enabled = auto_payout_enabled` | **also require `is_real_money_enabled()`** before build/broadcast |
+| Auto payout (Tron) | `supabase/functions/payout-tron/index.ts:207` | `if (auto_payout_enabled !== 'true') return disabled` | **also require master gate** |
+| Hot→cold sweep | `supabase/functions/sweep-hot-to-cold/index.ts` | (treasury op) | gate if it can move user-owed funds |
+| C74 → USDT swap | `supabase/functions/process-swap/index.ts` → `atomic_portfolio_swap` RPC | `c74_swap_settings.enabled` | **require master gate** on any USDT-realizing swap |
+
+## 2. Inbound — deposit crediting (money in)
+
+| Path | File | Current gate | Add |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| PSP settlement (Razorpay) | `supabase/functions/razorpay-webhook/index.ts` (idempotent credit from `deposit_requests`, ~line 128) | signature + deposit row only | **require master gate before credit** |
+| Razorpay order create | `supabase/functions/create-razorpay-order/index.ts:54` | `payment_gateways` enabled | gate at order create |
+| CCAvenue | `create-ccavenue-order` / `ccavenue-response` | gateway config | gate |
+| Fiat topup | `create-fiat-topup` / `verify-fiat-topup` | topup row | gate before credit |
+| Manual UPI credit | `supabase/functions/admin-credit-upi/index.ts` | admin auth | gate before credit |
+| On-chain deposit crediting | `verify-crypto-deposits`, `scan-user-deposits`, `cron-scan-deposits`, `deposit-watcher-{btc,ton,tron}` | per-chain `*_deposits_enabled` | **require master gate before crediting `casino_wallets`** |
+
+## 3. Client (advisory only — never the enforcement boundary)
+
+| Path | File · line | Role |
+|---|---|---|
+| Demo→live deposit redirect | `src/pages/ig/IgDemoDeposit.tsx:42` (`mode==='live' → /deposit`) | UX routing hint only |
+| `mode` read | `src/hooks/usePlatformMode.ts:16` | UX |
+| Crypto-deposit enable hint | `src/pages/ig/IgCryptoDeposit.tsx:82` (`evm_deposits_enabled`) | UX |
+| Admin flag panels | `AdminGoLive.tsx`, `AdminPaymentGateways.tsx`, `AdminWithdrawalsQueue.tsx`, `AdminKyc.tsx`, `AdminRealMoneyOps.tsx` | operator controls / reporting |
+
+The client `mode` redirect is **not** a security boundary — the authoritative
+block is server-side crediting/payout, which is why every row in §1–§2 is a
+server path.
+
+## 4. Authoritative choke-point (recommended)
+
+Rather than N scattered edits, funnel enforcement through the DB layer where the
+money actually moves:
+
+- Wrap the **idempotent deposit-credit RPC** (used by razorpay-webhook /
+  admin-credit-upi / deposit watchers) and **`atomic_portfolio_swap`** and the
+  **withdrawal-execution** path with `is_real_money_enabled()` (fail-closed).
+- Keep the **edge-function early-return** checks (§1–§2) as the first, cheap
+  line; the DB checks are the backstop that holds even if a function is called
+  directly.
+- Read-only RPCs (reconciliation, reporting, admin overviews) are **never**
+  gated.
+
+## 5. Test coverage (this change set)
+
+`src/test/real-money-gate.contract.test.ts` encodes the gate **contract** as an
+executable spec (self-contained reference predicate mirroring the future DB
+helper — imports no production code, changes no behavior):
+
+- **Fail-closed parse:** only the exact string `'true'` ⇒ ON; `undefined`,
+  `null`, `''`, `'false'`, `'FALSE'`, `'0'`, `'1'`, `'yes'` ⇒ OFF.
+- **Money-in blocked** when master OFF, regardless of the per-rail deposit flag.
+- **Money-out blocked** when master OFF, regardless of `auto_payout_enabled`.
+- **Defense in depth:** master ON ⇒ action allowed **iff** the rail flag is also on.
+- **Read-only always allowed**, both states.
+
+These tests define the behavior the real implementation (DB helper + wiring)
+must satisfy at review/apply time. They run in the existing `vitest` suite and
+touch no money path.
+
+---
+
+**Bottom line:** the master gate's value is entirely in the wiring — §1 and §2
+are the exact server sites that must call `is_real_money_enabled()`, §4 is the
+recommended single choke-point, and §5 is the executable contract. Applied later
+only under review; nothing here changes production now.
