Option A #3. Traces withdrawal_auto_approve (true, $100) and kyc_auto_approve
(true) end to end, with a policy matrix and verdict.

Key findings:
- request_crypto_withdrawal gates creation (KYC + apply_ledger_entry, which
  throws E_DEMO_MODE in demo mode -> mode is the de-facto money-out gate).
- admin-casino approve_withdrawal is the real on-chain broadcast; gated by
  admin role + fresh admin-PIN (<5min) + auto-path $100 cap, but NOT by
  real_money_enabled or mode.
- withdrawal_auto_approve is client-side only (needs a live admin PIN session);
  kyc_auto_approve auto-passes 18+/non-duplicate identity with no doc check.
- No bypass path: the only broadcaster requires admin+fresh PIN.

Verdict: safe as currently configured in practice (no autonomous payout: dual-
factor human gate + empty queue + $0 hot wallet + operator payouts OFF), but
three MUST-change-before-launch items: withdrawal_auto_approve OFF,
kyc_auto_approve OFF/real verification, and wire approve_withdrawal into the
master gate. Corrects CODEPATHS §1 to add the approve_withdrawal gate site.

Read-only: no flags flipped, no approvals changed, no SQL mutation, no money
moved. UI freeze baseline (d0e80ed) unchanged.
