+# Secrets Migration Plan — config tables → env / Vault
+
+**Status:** DESIGN / REVIEW ONLY — no SQL run, no secrets moved, no policy
+changed, no values exposed. Zero production change.
+**Companion to:** `REAL-MONEY-READINESS-AUDIT.md` (§ security notes)
+**Method:** read-only inspection of names/sizes (never values), RLS policies,
+grants, and how edge functions consume each secret.
+
+---
+
+## 0. Headline
+
+The codebase **already has the right pattern**: the most sensitive secrets live
+in **edge env / Vault / the locked `gateway_secrets` table**, and DB config
+values are **fallbacks** (`getGatewaySecret(...) || Deno.env.get(...) ||
+<plaintext>`). Two things remain: (1) **remove the plaintext DB fallbacks** so
+there is a single source of truth, and (2) **fix one over-broad RLS policy on
+`site_config`** that makes every row anon-readable.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Where secrets already live correctly (env / Vault) — keep
+
+Confirmed via `Deno.env.get(...)` usage:
+- **Wallet custody:** `HD_WALLET_MASTER_SEED`, `HOT_TRC20`, `COLD_TRC20`,
+  `HOT_BSC_EXPECTED`. `platform_wallets.private_key_encrypted` is **NULL for all
+  4 wallets** — no keys in DB. ✓ (derived via `ledger-vault-token` /
+  `resolve*HotWalletPk`).
+- **PSP:** `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET`, `RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET`, `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID`,
+  `CCAVENUE_ENCRYPTION_KEY`, `CCAVENUE_ACCESS_CODE`, `CCAVENUE_MERCHANT_ID`.
+- **Cron:** `CRON_SECRET` (used by reconcile-runner, anomaly-watchdog, admin-alert…).
+- **iGaming:** `IGAMING_SECRET`, `IGAMING_TOKEN`, `IGAMING_PROXY_URL/USER/PASS`.
+- **OTP / AI / RPC:** `OTP_HASH_SECRET`, `OTP_HASH_PEPPER`, `ANTHROPIC/OPENAI/GEMINI/DID_API_KEY`, `ALCHEMY_*_RPC`.
+- **`gateway_secrets` table:** RLS on, **no anon access** — the correct DB secret
+  store; the code prefers it first (`getGatewaySecret`).
+
+## 2. Current protection status of the DB config tables
+
+| Table | RLS read policy | Effect | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `platform_settings` | anon read **denylist**: `key !~* '(secret\|token\|password\|private\|mnemonic\|seed\|_rpc$\|webhook\|api_key)'` | `deposit_cron_token`, `scan_cron_secret` **blocked** from anon; rates/flags/UPI readable | 🟠 OK but denylist is fragile |
+| `site_config` | anon read **`using (true)`** | **every row anon-readable**, incl. `payment_gateways` (live `key_id`) and `bank_details` | 🔴 over-broad — main finding |
+| `gateway_secrets` | RLS on, **no policy** (deny-all to anon) | locked; service/definer only | 🟢 correct |
+
+**Key point:** the cron secrets in `platform_settings` are already **not**
+anon-exposed (blocked by the key-name regex). The genuine exposure is
+`site_config`'s blanket `using(true)`.
+
+## 3. Remaining plaintext DB values to migrate / clean up
+
+*(names + sizes only; values never read)*
+
+| Item | Location | Size | Also in env? | Action |
+|---|---|--:|---|---|
+| `deposit_cron_token` | `platform_settings` | 48 B | `CRON_SECRET` exists | migrate consumers → `CRON_SECRET`, then delete key |
+| `scan_cron_secret` | `platform_settings` | 48 B | `CRON_SECRET` exists | `payout-tron` still reads this from DB (`:120`) → switch to `CRON_SECRET`, then delete |
+| `payment_gateways.razorpay.key_id` (+any secret sub-fields) | `site_config` | 209 B blob | `RAZORPAY_KEY_ID` / gateway_secrets | strip credential sub-fields from the blob; keep only `enabled/mode/rate` |
+| `igaming_proxy_url` | `gateway_secrets` | 95 B | `IGAMING_PROXY_URL` env | duplicative → drop from DB, rely on env |
+| `bank_details` | `site_config` | 85 B | — | display data, but tighten via §4 RLS so it isn't blanket-anon |
+| `platform_upi_id` / `platform_upi_ids` | `platform_settings` | 14/18 B | — | display data (semi-public); acceptable, keep readable intentionally |
+
+`payment_gateway_keys` table is **empty** — nothing to migrate.
+
+## 4. Target architecture
+
+**Source-of-truth order (already the code's preference):**
+`Deno.env` (edge secrets) → `gateway_secrets` (locked table, service/definer only)
+→ ~~plaintext in `platform_settings`/`site_config`~~ (remove).
+
+- Runtime secrets (keys, tokens, seeds, webhook/cron secrets) → **edge env** (or
+  `gateway_secrets` for operator-rotatable ones).
+- Non-secret config (rates, caps, flags, display bank/UPI) → stays in
+  `platform_settings`/`site_config`, but behind **allowlist** RLS.
+- Remove every plaintext credential fallback so a DB read can never return a secret.
+
+## 5. Proposed changes — FOR REVIEW, NOT APPLIED
+
+```sql
+-- ⛔ REVIEW ONLY — do not execute outside an approved window.
+
+-- 5a. Tighten site_config read policy: replace blanket `using(true)` with a
+--     non-secret allowlist (mirrors platform_settings' approach).
+--     Confirm every key an anon client legitimately needs is listed first.
+-- drop policy "site_config public read" on public.site_config;
+-- create policy "site_config public read nonsecret" on public.site_config
+--   for select to anon, authenticated
+--   using (key in ('welcome_message','site_message','first_deposit','invite_bonus',
+--                  'currency_lang','game_providers','provider_config','web_colors',
+--                  'evm_deposits_enabled','btc_deposits_enabled','ton_deposits_enabled'));
+--   -- NOTE: 'payment_gateways' and 'bank_details' intentionally excluded;
+--   --       serve those via an authenticated RPC that returns only public fields.
+
+-- 5b. After consumers read RAZORPAY_KEY_ID from env/gateway_secrets, strip the
+--     credential from the site_config blob (keep enabled/mode/rate only).
+-- update site_config
+--    set value = (value #- '{gateways,razorpay,key_id}')
+--  where key='payment_gateways';
+
+-- 5c. After payout-tron switches to CRON_SECRET, delete the DB cron secrets.
+-- delete from platform_settings where key in ('deposit_cron_token','scan_cron_secret');
+
+-- 5d. Drop the duplicative proxy URL (IGAMING_PROXY_URL is in env).
+-- delete from gateway_secrets where name='igaming_proxy_url';
+```
+
+**Code changes (separate, reviewed PR — not in this doc):**
+- `payout-tron/index.ts:120` — read `Deno.env.get("CRON_SECRET")` instead of
+  `platform_settings.scan_cron_secret`.
+- Any consumer of `deposit_cron_token` — switch to `CRON_SECRET`.
+- Ensure `create-razorpay-order` / `razorpay-webhook` no longer need the
+  `site_config` `key_id` fallback (env/gateway_secrets present) before 5b.
+
+## 6. Pre-flight checks
+
+```sql
+-- Confirm env-first is in place so removing DB fallbacks won't break anything:
+--  (manual) supabase secrets list  → RAZORPAY_KEY_ID, RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET,
+--           RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET, CRON_SECRET, IGAMING_PROXY_URL present.
+-- Confirm no anon-critical key is dropped by the 5a allowlist:
+select key from site_config
+ where key not in ('welcome_message','site_message','first_deposit','invite_bonus',
+                   'currency_lang','game_providers','provider_config','web_colors',
+                   'evm_deposits_enabled','btc_deposits_enabled','ton_deposits_enabled');
+--  → review each remaining key (payment_gateways, bank_details) and confirm the
+--    client no longer reads it directly (moves to an authenticated RPC).
+```
+
+## 7. Post-change verification
+
+```sql
+-- site_config no longer blanket-readable:
+select has_table_privilege('anon','public.site_config','SELECT') as anon_has_grant;  -- still true (grant),
+-- but policy now restricts rows; verify a secret-bearing row is not returned as anon:
+--   (run as anon in a separate check) select value from site_config where key='payment_gateways'; -> 0 rows
+select (value ? 'gateways') as still_has_gateways,
+       (value #> '{gateways,razorpay}') ? 'key_id' as key_id_present   -- expect false after 5b
+from site_config where key='payment_gateways';
+select count(*) from platform_settings where key in ('deposit_cron_token','scan_cron_secret');  -- expect 0
+select count(*) from gateway_secrets where name='igaming_proxy_url';  -- expect 0
+```
+Then functionally verify: Razorpay order create + webhook still work (env),
+cron-triggered functions still authenticate (CRON_SECRET), deposits page still
+shows bank/UPI (via the new authenticated RPC).
+
+## 8. Rollback
+
+```sql
+-- ⛔ REVIEW ONLY
+-- restore the previous site_config read policy:
+-- drop policy "site_config public read nonsecret" on public.site_config;
+-- create policy "site_config public read" on public.site_config for select
+--   to anon, authenticated using (true);
+-- (5b/5c/5d are destructive deletes — restore from the pre-change JSON backup
+--  captured in the change window, not from this doc.)
+```
+> Before applying 5b–5d, capture a JSON backup of the affected rows so rollback
+> is exact.
+
+## 9. Marker
+
+**DO NOT APPLY.** Design + impact analysis only — no SQL executed, no policy
+changed, no secret moved or deleted, no value exposed in this document. The main
+security win is §5a (close `site_config`'s blanket read); §5b–5d remove redundant
+plaintext once env/Vault is confirmed as the single source of truth. UI freeze
+baseline (`d0e80ed`) unchanged.
-- 
