+# Treasury Funding & Readiness — assessment
+
+**Status:** READ-ONLY assessment — no money moved, no flags flipped, no SQL
+mutation. Zero production change.
+**Companion to:** `REAL-MONEY-READINESS-AUDIT.md` (§3, §6), `RECONCILIATION-DRIFT-INVESTIGATION.md`
+**Method:** `SELECT`-only against project `smcwrriaraptzjhqdktg`.
+
+> **Important caveat:** custody figures below are **DB-recorded**
+> (`platform_wallets.balance` / `native_balance`), refreshed by the
+> `treasury-balances` edge function — they may lag actual on-chain balances. A
+> real go-live gate must verify **live on-chain** custody, not just these rows.
+
+---
+
+## 0. Verdict
+
+🔴 **Treasury is NOT funded for launch.** The wallets that actually pay user
+withdrawals (hot / cold) hold **$0**, there is **no native gas** anywhere, and
+there is **no segregated reserve** backing user liabilities. At current scale
+this is trivially fixable, but structurally the operational treasury is empty.
+This is another independent reason real money must stay **OFF**.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Money position (point-in-time)
+
+### Liabilities — what the platform owes users
+| Currency | Wallets | Liability | Deposited (ever) | Withdrawn (ledger) | Quarantined |
+|---|--:|--:|--:|--:|--:|
+| USDT | 96 | **$23.48** | $13.95 | $24.14 | 1 |
+| USD | 1 | $0 | $0 | $0 | 0 |
+
+**Total user liability: $23.48.** Note: only **$13.95** was ever really
+*deposited*; the residual balance is largely **house-credited** (wins on
+free-play / bonuses), so true deposited-and-unwithdrawn exposure is even smaller.
+`total_withdrawn` ($24.14) is a ledger counter and does **not** reconcile to
+on-chain — **$0 crypto withdrawals have settled** (the 2 historical were
+rejected/refunded), consistent with test-scale data.
+
+### C74 real-money obligation
+| Item | Value |
+|---|---|
+| C74 → USDT swap | **enabled**, pool **$1.56**, $0.01/C74, $5/user/day cap |
+
+Max additional real-money obligation from C74 redemption is bounded by the pool
+(**$1.56**). C74 gullak/energy balances are token-denominated (internal), not
+direct USDT liabilities.
+
+**Total real-money obligations ≈ $23.48 + $1.56 = ~$25.04 (upper bound).**
+
+### Custody — assets held (DB-recorded)
+| Chain | Wallet | Active | USDT | Native (gas) |
+|---|---|:--:|--:|--:|
+| BASE | c74_reserve | yes | **$9.84** | 0 |
+| TRON | c74_reserve | no | $0 | 0 |
+| TRC20 | cold | yes | **$0** | 0 |
+| TRC20 | **hot** | yes | **$0** | **0** |
+
+**Total custody: $9.84 — all in the C74-reserve wallet.** The **hot** wallet
+(which pays user withdrawals) and **cold** wallet hold **$0**, and **every wallet
+has 0 native gas**.
+
+### Treasury (operator fees) & reserve — ledger
+| Ledger | Total |
+|---|--:|
+| `treasury_ledger` (fees: deposit $13.95 + withdrawal $23.93) | $37.88 |
+| `c74_reserve_ledger` | $11.41 |
+
+These are **accounting entries**, not proof of segregated held funds.
+
+### In flight
+Pending withdrawals: **0**. Settled crypto withdrawals: **$0**.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Solvency analysis
+
+| Measure | Value |
+|---|--:|
+| User liabilities (USDT) | $23.48 |
+| + C74 swap obligation (pool) | $1.56 |
+| **Total obligations** | **~$25.04** |
+| Custody (DB-recorded, all wallets) | $9.84 |
+| **Coverage ratio (custody ÷ obligations)** | **~39%** |
+| Custody in the withdrawal-paying **hot** wallet | **$0 (0%)** |
+| Native gas for broadcasts | **$0 — cannot send even if funded** |
+
+- **Under-collateralized** at the aggregate level (~39%), and **0% in the wallet
+  that actually pays withdrawals**.
+- The $9.84 that exists is **earmarked C74 reserve** (BASE), not user-liability
+  custody — so effective user-withdrawal backing is **$0**.
+- Ties to the audit's $23.48-vs-$9.84 gap: **real, but micro-scale and structural
+  (empty operational wallets), and entirely separate** from the $21.7k projection
+  drift — which #4 already proved is a non-liability artifact.
+
+---
+
+## 3. What is required before launch (funding & segregation)
+
+1. 💰 **Fund the hot wallet** with USDT ≥ expected withdrawal volume + buffer, and
+   **native gas** (TRX for TRC20; ETH/BASE for BEP20/BASE) so broadcasts can run.
+2. 🏦 **Fund & segregate a reserve** ≥ **100%** of user liabilities + the C74 swap
+   pool, held **separately from operator revenue** (do not count `treasury_ledger`
+   fees as backing).
+3. ❄️ **Cold-storage policy** for excess over the hot-wallet float
+   (`sweep-hot-to-cold` exists) with documented thresholds.
+4. 🧮 **Operator/user separation** — keep operator revenue ($37.88 fees) out of
+   the liability-backing custody; only user-owed funds count toward coverage.
+5. 🔗 **Live on-chain verification** as a launch gate (not DB-recorded balances) —
+   wire it into the L5 solvency view (`admin_real_money_ops_overview` already
+   models the picture) and into reconciliation.
+6. 🚦 **Solvency policy + kill switch** — require custody ≥ obligations at all
+   times; if the ratio drops below threshold, the master gate (design #1) trips
+   real money OFF automatically.
+
+---
+
+## 4. How this closes the audit
+
+Treasury is the last of the seven Option-A items. Combined result:
+
+- Inbound is configured **live** (mode/Razorpay/rails) but **outbound automated
+  payout + emission are OFF**, and now **treasury is confirmed unfunded** — so
+  even the manual/human payout path has **nothing to pay** ($0 hot wallet, no gas).
+- Real-money launch requires **all** external gates: **license · PSP approval ·
+  funded & segregated treasury · compliance** — plus the internal fixes queued in
+  #1–#6 (unify the master gate, inbound-OFF baseline, auto-approve policy off,
+  RLS, secrets). **None** is satisfied today.
+
+**Recommendation:** keep real money OFF; do not fund the treasury for live
+operation until license + PSP approval are in hand and the #1–#6 changes are
+applied under review. Funding an unlicensed live treasury would be the riskiest
+possible step.
+
+---
+
+## 5. No changes made
+
+Read-only assessment only — no money moved, no wallet funded, no flag changed,
+no SQL mutation. Figures are DB-recorded (verify live on-chain before any launch
+decision). UI freeze baseline (`d0e80ed`) unchanged.
