+## 8b. Key rotation plan
+
+Migration is one-time; **rotation is ongoing**. Because the code reads
+**env / `gateway_secrets` first with a fallback chain**, most secrets can rotate
+**zero-downtime** by overlapping old+new during the cutover.
+
+**Cadence**
+- API keys / PSP keys / cron secret: **rotate quarterly**, and **immediately** on
+  suspected compromise or staff offboarding.
+- Wallet seed / hot-wallet key: rotate only on compromise or key-custody change
+  (high-cost — requires a funds sweep, see below).
+- Every rotation is **dual-control** and written to `audit_logs`.
+
+**Per-secret procedure (all zero-downtime unless noted):**
+
+| Secret | Rotate where | Cutover pattern |
+|---|---|---|
+| `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET` / `KEY_ID` | Razorpay dashboard → new keys | set new env → redeploy `create-razorpay-order` → verify an order → revoke old |
+| `RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET` | Razorpay dashboard | Razorpay signs with the new secret after save; update env **before** saving in Razorpay, or accept both during a short window in `razorpay-webhook` |
+| `CRON_SECRET` | edge secret + DB trigger senders | temporarily accept **old OR new** in the verifier, set new env everywhere, then drop old |
+| `gateway_secrets` rows | `admin-gateway-secrets` fn (admin + PIN) | update row (writer bypasses RLS); reads pick it up immediately (`getGatewaySecret` first) |
+| `IGAMING_SECRET` / `TOKEN` | provider portal + env | overlap if provider supports two keys; else brief maintenance window |
+| **`HD_WALLET_MASTER_SEED` / hot key** | **generate new wallet** | **NOT zero-downtime**: derive new wallet → `sweep-hot-to-cold` old balance → fund new hot → update env → point `derive-user-wallet` / deposit addresses forward → retire old. Run only in a supervised window. |
+
+**Zero-downtime rule:** during any rotation, the verifier/consumer must accept
+**old ∪ new** for the overlap, then the old value is removed and re-verified.
+
+**Post-rotation verification**
+- PSP: create a test order + replay a webhook → credited path works.
+- Cron: trigger a cron function → authenticates with the new secret.
+- Wallet: a test deposit derives to the new wallet; a test payout broadcasts.
+- Confirm the **old** secret is now rejected everywhere.
+
+**Rollback:** keep the previous value available for the overlap window only; if a
+new secret misbehaves, revert env to the prior value (still accepted during
+overlap) and re-verify — no data change needed.
+
 ## 9. Marker
 
