@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+# External Gates Checklist — License · PSP · Treasury
+
+**Status:** business-readiness reference. **Not legal advice.** Every gate below
+needs a real third-party document and a qualified gaming/regulatory lawyer in the
+target jurisdiction. Nothing here activates real money; it tracks what must be
+*truly* in hand before Runbook Steps 1–4 can go green.
+
+> ⚠️ **Reality check.** A company + a built platform is ~95% of the *engineering*,
+> but 0% of the *authorization*. Real-money gambling is a licensed activity. You
+> must serve **only** markets you are licensed for and **geo-block** everyone else.
+> Operating without the right license exposes **you** to frozen funds, seized
+> accounts, and criminal liability — regardless of how the tech is built.
+
+---
+
+## Gate 1 — Corporate  ✅ (evidence on file)
+
+| Item | Needed | Status |
+|---|---|---|
+| Legal entity | Incorporation / LLC operating agreement | ✅ **US LLC on file** (EIN redacted) |
+| Registered address / registered agent | On the formation docs | ✅ (in the agreement) |
+| Business bank account | Statement / confirmation | ⬜ verify |
+
+**Note:** a US LLC proves the *entity* exists. It does **not** authorize
+gambling. A generic US LLC (Delaware / Wyoming / Atlas-style) is explicitly
+**not** a gaming licensee, and US entities carry **higher** gambling-law exposure
+(federal Wire Act / UIGEA + state-by-state prohibition), not lower.
+
+---
+
+## Gate 2 — Gaming license  ⬜ (the decisive gate)
+
+You cannot pick "activate" — you pick a **jurisdiction and market**, then get its
+license. Answer these first, with counsel:
+
+1. **Which players will you serve?** (country/state) — this determines everything.
+2. **US players?** Then you need **state-by-state licenses** (e.g. NJ/PA/MI/…),
+   each with large capital, local presence, background checks. Most US states
+   prohibit online casino outright. A US LLC does **not** grant this.
+3. **Non-US, licensed-offshore route?** Operators commonly license in a
+   gaming jurisdiction (e.g. Malta MGA, Isle of Man, Curaçao, etc.). Each has
+   its own capital, KYC/AML, responsible-gaming, and **mandatory geo-blocking of
+   prohibited markets** (which includes the US and many others).
+
+**Evidence that turns this gate green:** a valid **license certificate** naming
+your entity, the permitted products (casino/slots/etc.), and the permitted
+territories — plus your **geo-blocking policy** matching it.
+
+**Hard stops:** no license · license doesn't cover your product · you'd be
+serving players outside the licensed territory. Any of these ⇒ do not proceed.
+
+---
+
+## Gate 3 — PSP / payment approval  ⬜
+
+Payments for gambling need a processor that **approves gaming** under the correct
+merchant category (MCC 7995). Generic onboarding does **not** count.
+
+| Rail | Reality |
+|---|---|
+| Standard Stripe / generic Razorpay / PayPal | **Prohibit gambling** by ToS — will freeze/terminate |
+| Razorpay (currently configured) | Needs Razorpay's **explicit gaming approval** for your entity + license; India has its own gaming restrictions |
+| Gaming-specialist PSPs | Exist, but require your **license** first + full AML/KYC onboarding |
+| Crypto (USDT — already built) | No "approval" per se, but you still owe **AML/KYC, sanctions screening, and Travel-Rule** compliance; can't skip diligence |
+
+### About Binance / exchanges (you asked)
+- **Binance is a crypto exchange, not a PSP and not a treasury.** Customers can't
+  "pay via Binance" into your casino as a compliant processor, and routing
+  gambling settlement through a personal/business exchange account **violates
+  exchange ToS** (gambling restrictions) → **account freeze** risk.
+- It can be a **liquidity source** — you buy USDT on a KYC'd exchange to fund your
+  own custody wallet — but keep **source-of-funds records**; it is not the
+  operating treasury.
+- Your platform already has the **correct custody** (HD hot/cold wallets). The
+  treasury should be **those wallets**, funded from a documented, compliant
+  source — never operated out of an exchange login.
+
+**Evidence that turns this gate green:** written PSP approval for real-money
+gaming (entity + license + settlement account), and/or a documented, AML-compliant
+crypto flow.
+
+---
+
+## Gate 4 — Funded treasury + reserve invariant GREEN  ⬜
+
+From `TREASURY-READINESS.md` §3b/§3c. Currently 🔴 **BREACHED** (custody $0).
+
+**Invariant:** `liquid_custody ≥ user_liabilities + c74_swap_pool` — always.
+
+**Minimum funding:**
+```
+hot_float    = max(expected_daily_withdrawals × S, hot_floor) + gas_reserve
+cold_reserve = (user_liabilities + swap_pool) × R − hot_USDT      (R ≥ 1.00, buffer 1.05–1.10)
+```
+
+| Item | Needed |
+|---|---|
+| Cold reserve funded (≥100% obligations) | ⬜ on-chain, verified |
+| Hot float funded | ⬜ |
+| Gas funded (TRX / native) | ⬜ |
+| Funds from a **documented, compliant source** (not commingled) | ⬜ |
+| Live on-chain balance verification | ⬜ |
+| Invariant GREEN | ⬜ (activation RPC will refuse `E_INSOLVENT` until then) |
+
+---
+
+## Gate 5 — Banking · compliance · responsible gaming  ⬜
+
+| Item | Needed |
+|---|---|
+| Operating bank account that permits gaming settlement | ⬜ |
+| AML/KYC program (real identity verification — not auto-approve) | ⬜ (see #3 auto-approve OFF) |
+| Sanctions / PEP screening | ⬜ |
+| Responsible-gaming controls (already built: limits, self-exclusion) | ✅ product · ⬜ policy sign-off |
+| Geo-blocking of prohibited markets | ⬜ must match the license |
+| Data protection / player-funds segregation per license | ⬜ |
+
+---
+
+## Evidence intake — what proves each gate
+
+| # | Gate | Green when you have… |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Corporate | ✅ entity docs (on file) + business bank |
+| 2 | License | licence certificate (entity · products · territories) + geo policy |
+| 3 | PSP | written gaming approval and/or AML-compliant crypto flow |
+| 4 | Treasury | on-chain proof custody ≥ obligations + funding source records |
+| 5 | Compliance | AML program, screening, RG sign-off, geo-block config |
+
+**None of these can be self-certified.** Each needs a real external document. When
+all five are genuinely green, and only then, the Runbook (Steps 1–13) drives the
+supervised activation — ending with an authorized admin typing `ENABLE REAL
+MONEY`, with the server's reserve-invariant guard as the last line.
+
+---
+
+*Not legal advice. Engage a licensed gaming/regulatory attorney and a compliance
+/ AML specialist for your target jurisdiction before proceeding.*
-- 
