+# Social-Casino Mode — Design (coin purchase, no cash-out)
+
+**Status:** design / product spec. **Not legal advice** — a social-casino /
+coin-purchase model still needs a compliant payment processor and legal
+confirmation for the target market (see §4). Nothing here is applied; real-money
+cash-out stays permanently OFF.
+
+**Model:** players **buy virtual coins** with real money → play → coins are for
+entertainment only and **can never be cashed out, withdrawn, traded, or redeemed
+for money.** No real-world prize ⇒ generally **not gambling** ⇒ no gaming license
+required. This is the direction chosen over a licensed real-money casino.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Why this avoids a gaming license
+
+Gambling generally requires all three: **consideration + chance + prize**. This
+model removes the **prize** — coins have no monetary value and no cash-out path.
+Remove the prize and chance-based play is generally a game, not gambling.
+
+**The legal line is the cash-out. It must be absolute.**
+
+## 2. Hard rules (non-negotiable — these keep it legal)
+
+1. **No cash-out. Ever.** No withdrawal, no crypto payout, no C74→USDT (or any
+   token→money) redemption, no operator payout to players, **no secondary market
+   / peer trading of coins for money.** There must be **no code path** that turns
+   coins back into money.
+2. **Coins / C74 = closed virtual currency.** No real-world value, not
+   transferable for money, not an "investment." (Otherwise it risks being a
+   security or gambling instrument.)
+3. **Clear disclaimers everywhere** the user sees currency or "wins":
+   *"Coins have no monetary value and cannot be exchanged for cash or withdrawn.
+   Free-to-play entertainment only. 18+."*
+4. **No implication of real winnings.** Never say "win real money", "cash prize",
+   "withdraw your winnings", etc. "Win coins" only.
+5. **Purchases are final** (virtual goods) — clear refund/terms policy.
+
+## 3. What changes vs the current build
+
+| Area | Now | Social-casino target |
+|---|---|---|
+| Cash-out (withdraw / crypto / swap-to-USDT / payout) | gated by master flag | **permanently disabled — no enable path at all** |
+| `real_money_enabled` (for payouts) | OFF | stays OFF forever; the activation control is **removed/inert** for this mode |
+| Deposit | real-money deposit ("mode=live") | **reframe as "Buy Coins"** (virtual-goods purchase), gated behind a compliant PSP (see §4) |
+| C74 → USDT swap | enabled ($1.56 pool) | **disabled** (it's a cash-out path) |
+| Copy / UI | "deposit / withdraw / winnings" | "Buy coins / coin balance / you won coins" + disclaimers |
+| Currency | USDT-denominated balance | virtual **coins** (no monetary value) |
+| Age / responsible-play | built | keep (18+, limits) — good practice even for social |
+
+**Gate design for this mode:** split the switches —
+- **cash-out: hard OFF** (removed, not flag-gated — there is nothing to turn on),
+- **coin purchase: a separate `coin_purchase_enabled` flag**, ON only once a
+  compliant PSP + legal clearance exist (§4).
+
+## 4. Remaining external gates (lower than a casino, but NOT zero)
+
+Coin purchase = **taking real money in**, so it still needs:
+
+1. **A payment processor that permits social-casino / virtual-goods coin sales.**
+   Many PSPs and both app stores restrict "social casino" specifically — Apple
+   App Store & Google Play have named social-casino policies; card processors
+   vary. Confirm the processor's written policy for *your* content.
+2. **Legal confirmation for the target market.** Critically for **India**: a
+   *paid, chance-based* social game is **legally ambiguous** even without cash-out
+   — some states/regulators scrutinise paid entry to chance games, and the **28%
+   GST on "online money gaming"** may be argued to apply. **No cash-out does not
+   automatically make paid chance-play legal in India.** Get an Indian gaming +
+   tax lawyer to confirm before taking real money for coins.
+3. **Consumer / advertising rules** — no misleading "winnings", clear virtual-only
+   terms, loot-box/simulated-gambling rules in some jurisdictions.
+
+**Safest sequencing:** ship the free-play experience with **all cash-out removed**
+and clear disclaimers first (needs nothing external); enable **coin purchase**
+only after the PSP policy + legal sign-off above.
+
+## 5. Implementation plan (safe parts first — I can build these now)
+
+**Phase A — lock the legal line (no external dependency):**
+- Hard-disable every cash-out path (withdraw UI, crypto withdrawal, C74→USDT
+  swap, operator-payout-to-player) — remove, not merely flag-off.
+- Add the virtual-currency **disclaimers** across purchase / balance / win screens.
+- Reframe copy: "Buy Coins", "coin balance", "you won coins" — remove "withdraw /
+  real money / cash prize".
+
+**Phase B — coin purchase (after §4 PSP + legal):**
+- `coin_purchase_enabled` flag (default OFF); wire a compliant virtual-goods PSP;
+  "Buy Coins" packs; purchase → credit virtual coins (no cash-out counterpart).
+
+## 6. Current status
+
+- ✅ `real_money_enabled` OFF → cash-out already blocked at the ledger.
+- ✅ Free-play gameplay, coins, missions, VIP all work as virtual.
+- ⬜ Phase A hardening (remove cash-out paths + disclaimers) — ready to build.
+- ⬜ Phase B coin purchase — pending compliant PSP + legal sign-off (§4).
+
+*Not legal advice. Confirm the model with a gaming/consumer + tax lawyer for your
+market before enabling paid coin purchase.*
-- 
