+# Platform ↔ Third-Party Cash-Out — Boundary Specification
+
+**Status:** design / compliance spec. **Not legal advice.** Nothing here is
+applied; `real_money_enabled` stays OFF; the platform performs no cash-out.
+**Companion to:** `SOCIAL-CASINO-MODE-DESIGN.md` §3b, `EXTERNAL-GATES-CHECKLIST.md`.
+
+> ## The one principle this whole document serves
+> **The platform is a social game engine with a closed virtual-coin ledger. It
+> never turns coins into money.** If cash-out is ever offered, it is operated by a
+> **separate, genuinely independent, appropriately licensed third party** under
+> **its own** funds, custody, and KYC/AML — across the hard boundary below.
+>
+> **This boundary is protective ONLY IF the separation is real.** If the "third
+> party" is the same operator in disguise, or the platform's chance-based play
+> feeds an automatic coin→cash pipe, regulators treat the **whole system** as
+> gambling and the platform as operating it (substance over form). A gaming
+> lawyer must confirm the structure before any coin↔cash link exists.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Roles & responsibilities
+
+| Party | Does | Never does |
+|---|---|---|
+| **Platform** | game engine; **virtual-coin ledger**; (Phase B) sells coins as virtual goods via PSP | hold cash-out float · convert coins→money · initiate/settle player payouts · custody redeemable balances |
+| **Virtual-goods PSP** | processes **coin purchases** (money **in**) under its own gaming/virtual-goods policy | — |
+| **Third-party cash-out provider** (only if pursued) | any real-money **out** to players, under **its own** license, custody, KYC/AML, sanctions, Travel-Rule | rely on the platform to be the licensed operator |
+| **Player** | buys coins; plays; holds **virtual coins with no monetary value** | withdraw coins from the platform (no such function) |
+
+## 2. The boundary line — explicit
+
+**Platform side (in scope):**
+- Gameplay, RNG/provably-fair, missions, VIP — all denominated in **virtual coins**.
+- A coin ledger that is **not** redeemable and has **no cash-out endpoint**.
+- (Phase B) "Buy Coins" — a one-way virtual-goods purchase (money in, coins out).
+
+**Outside the boundary (never platform-operated):**
+- Any conversion of coins → money.
+- Any custody of funds earmarked for player cash-out.
+- Any initiation, approval, or settlement of a player payout.
+
+There is **no code path** on the platform that performs, schedules, or
+auto-triggers a coin→cash conversion. Introducing one requires the §5 contract +
+§6 legal gate — off by default, out of scope until then.
+
+## 3. Data-flow
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+  P([Player])
+  PSP[[Virtual-goods PSP]]
+  PLAT[Platform: game engine + closed coin ledger]
+  TP[[Third-party cash-out provider — separately licensed]]
+
+  P -->|1 buy coins - real money| PSP
+  PSP -->|2 purchase confirmed| PLAT
+  PLAT -->|3 credit VIRTUAL coins| P
+  P -->|4 play - coins only| PLAT
+
+  subgraph BOUNDARY [hard boundary - no automatic coin to cash]
+    PLAT -. 5 read-only identity/eligibility ONLY, if contracted+legal .-> TP
+  end
+  TP -->|6 any real-money-out under ITS OWN license/custody/KYC-AML| P
+
+  classDef never stroke-dasharray:4 4;
+  class BOUNDARY never;
+```
+
+- Steps **1–4** are the whole platform: money **in** for coins, play in coins.
+- Step **5** crosses the boundary **only** if a licensed provider is contracted
+  and legally cleared — and carries **minimal, read-only** data (see §4), never a
+  "convert these coins to cash" instruction.
+- Step **6** is entirely the third party's regulated function; the platform does
+  not fund, initiate, or settle it.
+
+## 4. Data boundary — what may cross
+
+| Data | Crosses? | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| Player identifier (opaque/read-only) | only if contracted + legal | minimal; for the third party's own KYC match |
+| Eligibility signal (read-only) | only if contracted + legal | no coin balances "for conversion" |
+| **Coin balances as a cash instruction** | **never** | would create an automatic coin→cash pipe |
+| Player funds / cash-out float | **never** | platform holds none |
+| Payment credentials / secrets | **never** | each side holds its own |
+
+The platform is the **ledger of record for coins**; the third party is the ledger
+of record for any **cash**. There is **no shared writable balance** that both
+sides mutate.
+
+## 5. Fund custody & ownership
+
+- **Coin-purchase revenue** (Phase B) is **virtual-goods income** to the platform
+  entity — its own book, its own bank/PSP settlement. It is **not** a player
+  balance and **not** redeemable.
+- **Any cash-out funds** are the **third party's** — its own custody, its own
+  bank/wallet, its own reserve. The platform **never** holds them.
+- **No commingling:** coin-purchase proceeds and third-party cash-out funds are
+  **separate entities, separate accounts, separate books.** Commingling collapses
+  the boundary.
+
+## 6. KYC / AML / sanctions responsibility
+
+Responsibility follows **whoever moves real money** — never silently the platform:
+
+| Function | Owner |
+|---|---|
+| Coin purchase (money in) | the **PSP** + platform per the PSP's virtual-goods rules |
+| Cash-out (money out) | the **third party** — full KYC/AML, sanctions/PEP screening, Travel-Rule, record-keeping under its own license |
+| Player identity for cash-out | the **third party** (its regulated onboarding) |
+
+The contract must **state this allocation explicitly**; it cannot default onto
+the platform by silence.
+
+## 7. Contract requirements (what the third-party agreement must say)
+
+1. The provider is **independently owned/operated** and **holds the licenses**
+   required for real-money-out in each market it serves.
+2. The provider is the **operator of record** for cash-out; the platform is an
+   **integrator**, not the gambling operator.
+3. **KYC/AML/sanctions/Travel-Rule** obligations sit with the provider.
+4. **No automatic coin→cash** — any conversion is the provider's own regulated
+   act, not an instruction issued by the platform's game outcomes.
+5. **Funds separation & non-commingling**; independent custody; audit rights.
+6. **Liability & indemnity** allocation; data-protection terms; **termination /
+   geo-restriction** obligations matching each market's law.
+
+## 8. Couplings that COLLAPSE the boundary (prohibited)
+
+Any of these makes the whole system gambling operated by the platform:
+- An **automatic** coin→cash conversion, or the platform **instructing** payouts.
+- The platform **holding** redeemable-for-cash balances or cash-out float.
+- A **non-independent** "third party" (same beneficial owner, no real license).
+- **Revenue-share** structured so the platform effectively earns gambling
+  proceeds from player losses via the cash-out leg.
+- Marketing that ties platform play to **real cash winnings** ("win & withdraw").
+
+## 9. How to verify the boundary holds (audit)
+
+- **Code:** grep proves **no coin→cash / withdrawal / payout path** on the
+  platform is wired (search for withdrawal, payout, swap-to-USDT, redeem).
+- **Custody:** separate legal entities + separate accounts on file; no shared
+  balance table both sides write.
+- **Contracts:** the §7 agreement executed; third-party licenses on file.
+- **Legal:** written counsel opinion for each target market **before** any
+  coin↔cash link (India: see the checklist — paid chance-play is ambiguous even
+  with cash-out outsourced; 28% GST question).
+- **Flags:** `real_money_enabled` OFF; no `coin_purchase_enabled` until Phase B
+  gates met.
+
+## 10. Status
+
+- ✅ Platform provides **no** cash-out (ledger gate OFF); coins are virtual-only.
+- ⏸️ Phase A (platform-side lock + disclaimers) **on hold** until this boundary is
+  reviewed and legally confirmed.
+- ⬜ Phase B (coin purchase) — pending compliant PSP + legal.
+- ⬜ Phase C (third-party cash-out) — pending §7 contract + §6/§9 legal gate.
+
+*Not legal advice. The boundary is only protective with a genuinely independent,
+licensed third party and written legal confirmation for each market. Confirm with
+a gaming/consumer + tax lawyer before wiring any coin↔cash link. Nothing here is
+applied; real money OFF.*
-- 
