+# Third-Party Cash-Out Provider — Due-Diligence Checklist
+
+**Status:** evidence-intake checklist · **documentation only** · **Not legal advice.**
+**Companion to:** `PLATFORM-THIRDPARTY-BOUNDARY.md`, `SOCIAL-CASINO-MODE-DESIGN.md`,
+`docs/audits/2026-08-22-consolidated-readiness-register.md`.
+
+> 🔒 **Scope guard.** Nothing here is applied. No production change, no migration,
+> no deploy, no flag flip. `real_money_enabled` remains **OFF**. This checklist
+> gathers the evidence that must exist **before** the third-party cash-out route
+> can even be *considered* — it does not authorize anything.
+
+> ## The principle this checklist enforces
+> **A third party doing cash-out does NOT let the platform open its own money gate.**
+> `real_money_enabled` is the *platform's* control (real deposits credit, ledger
+> treats money as real) — enabling it needs the platform's **own** license + PSP +
+> funded treasury regardless of who does cash-out. And the third-party route is
+> protective **only if the separation is real and the provider is genuinely
+> independent and actually licensed** (substance over form). Every row below must
+> be **evidenced**, not asserted.
+
+Status legend: ⬜ not provided · 🟡 provided, under review · ✅ verified (by counsel/compliance).
+
+---
+
+## A. Provider legal entity & licensing
+
+| # | Item | Evidence required | Status |
+|---|------|-------------------|:--:|
+| A1 | **Legal entity & jurisdiction** | Certificate of incorporation; registered address/agent; ownership/UBO register | ⬜ |
+| A2 | **Genuine independence** | UBO + directors show **no common beneficial owner / control** with the platform entity; arm's-length proof | ⬜ |
+| A3 | **Valid license / regulatory registration** | The actual **license certificate** naming the provider entity; issuing regulator; validity dates; good-standing letter | ⬜ |
+| A4 | **License scope** | Written confirmation the license **permits the exact cash-out / money-transmission / e-money activity** in **each target market** (not a generic reg) | ⬜ |
+| A5 | **Permitted territories** | List of markets the license covers + provider's **geo-blocking** for the rest | ⬜ |
+
+## B. Contract & liability
+
+| # | Item | Evidence required | Status |
+|---|------|-------------------|:--:|
+| B1 | **Executed contract** | Signed agreement; provider is the **operator of record** for cash-out, platform is an **integrator** | ⬜ |
+| B2 | **Liability allocation & indemnity** | Clauses assigning regulatory/financial liability for cash-out to the provider; indemnity to the platform | ⬜ |
+| B3 | **No automatic coin→cash** | Contract states any conversion is the **provider's own regulated act**, not triggered by platform game outcomes | ⬜ |
+
+## C. Funds, custody & settlement
+
+| # | Item | Evidence required | Status |
+|---|------|-------------------|:--:|
+| C1 | **Who legally receives customer funds** | Documented: cash-out funds are the **provider's**, in the provider's own regulated accounts — **never** the platform's | ⬜ |
+| C2 | **Fund segregation / non-commingling** | Separate legal entities, separate bank/custody accounts, separate books; segregation attestation | ⬜ |
+| C3 | **Custody / key ownership** | Provider holds its own custody + signing keys for cash-out; platform holds **no** cash-out float or keys | ⬜ |
+| C4 | **Settlement & reconciliation** | Documented settlement cadence + reconciliation process + who signs off; ledger-of-record on each side | ⬜ |
+
+## D. Compliance ownership (KYC / AML / sanctions)
+
+| # | Item | Evidence required | Status |
+|---|------|-------------------|:--:|
+| D1 | **KYC/AML ownership** | Provider owns full KYC/AML for cash-out (its regulated program); contract states this explicitly | ⬜ |
+| D2 | **Customer onboarding responsibility** | Provider's regulated onboarding for anyone receiving cash-out (not the platform's auto-approve) | ⬜ |
+| D3 | **Sanctions / transaction monitoring** | Provider's sanctions/PEP screening + Travel-Rule + ongoing monitoring program; who is responsible | ⬜ |
+| D4 | **Data crossing the boundary** | Exactly what data passes (opaque identifier / eligibility only) — **never** coin balances "for conversion" or a cash instruction | ⬜ |
+
+## E. Operational controls
+
+| # | Item | Evidence required | Status |
+|---|------|-------------------|:--:|
+| E1 | **API permissions & withdrawal controls** | Least-privilege API scope; the platform cannot instruct/initiate a payout; provider-side approval controls | ⬜ |
+| E2 | **Audit logs & reporting** | Immutable logs both sides; agreed reporting; audit rights in the contract | ⬜ |
+| E3 | **Refund / chargeback / dispute** | Documented ownership + process for refunds/chargebacks/disputes | ⬜ |
+| E4 | **Incident / fraud handling** | Joint incident-response + fraud-handling runbook; notification SLAs | ⬜ |
+
+## F. Data, privacy & wind-down
+
+| # | Item | Evidence required | Status |
+|---|------|-------------------|:--:|
+| F1 | **Data / privacy responsibilities** | Data-protection terms; processor/controller roles; retention; cross-border transfer basis | ⬜ |
+| F2 | **Termination & wind-down** | Exit plan; customer-funds return; geo-restriction obligations on termination | ⬜ |
+
+## G. Independent legal confirmation
+
+| # | Item | Evidence required | Status |
+|---|------|-------------------|:--:|
+| G1 | **Independent legal opinion** | Written opinion (per target market) confirming the **separation is real** and the whole arrangement is **not** platform-operated gambling (substance over form) | ⬜ |
+| G2 | **Tax position** | Opinion on tax treatment (e.g. India 28% GST on online money gaming) for the arrangement | ⬜ |
+
+---
+
+## H. Evidence required before `real_money_enabled` can EVER be eligible
+
+> Completing A–G is **necessary but not sufficient**. The third-party route only
+> covers cash-out. The platform's **own** money-in and obligations still gate.
+
+Final eligibility for even *considering* activation requires **all** of:
+1. **This checklist (A–G) complete & counsel-verified** — provider independent, licensed, contracted, legally opined.
+2. **Platform license / approved real-money architecture** for taking money **in**.
+3. **PSP gaming approval** (money-in rail) verified.
+4. **Treasury verified** — on-chain hot/cold ≥ full user-liability coverage.
+5. **8/8 technical systems GREEN** (consolidated register §10 re-audit).
+6. **Dual-control change window** with rollback staged.
+
+Only when **1–6 are all true** does activation come up for consideration — and even
+then it is: change window → post-change 8/8 GREEN → an authorized admin runs
+`admin_set_real_money_enabled(true, 'ENABLE REAL MONEY')`, which itself refuses
+`E_INSOLVENT` unless custody ≥ obligations.
+
+**Any single ⬜ or unmet gate ⇒ NO-GO. `real_money_enabled` stays OFF.**
+
+---
+
+*Not legal advice. Engage qualified gaming/regulatory + tax counsel in each target
+market. Nothing here is applied; no production change; `real_money_enabled` OFF.*
-- 
