+# Real-Money Licensing Roadmap
+
+**Status:** orientation / planning doc · **documentation only** · **NOT legal advice.**
+**Companion to:** `EXTERNAL-GATES-CHECKLIST.md` (Gate 2), `PLATFORM-THIRDPARTY-BOUNDARY.md`,
+`THIRD-PARTY-CASHOUT-DUE-DILIGENCE-CHECKLIST.md`, the consolidated readiness register.
+
+> 🔒 **Scope guard.** Nothing here is applied; no production change; `real_money_enabled`
+> stays OFF. This maps *what a license path looks like* so counsel can be engaged
+> efficiently. **Costs/timelines are indicative ranges — verify every figure with a
+> licensed gaming/regulatory attorney in the target market.**
+
+> ## The first decision drives everything
+> **You do not "get a gaming license" — you pick a market, then get that market's
+> license.** Product (casino / slots / chance-based) + who your players are
+> together determine the regime, the cost, and whether it is even possible.
+
+---
+
+## 0. Where the platform is today (baseline)
+
+- Product = **chance-based casino/slots** (games of chance for money) — the hardest class to license.
+- Chosen product direction = **social-casino** (C74 virtual coins, **no platform cash-out**); any cash-out is a **separate licensed third party** (see boundary doc).
+- Target market discussed = **India**.
+- Real-money gate = **OFF**; treasury unfunded.
+
+Two independent tracks below. **Pick the market first**, then follow that track.
+
+---
+
+## Track A — India-facing real money  ⚠️ (highest difficulty)
+
+**The core legal reality (verify with Indian gaming counsel):**
+- India distinguishes **games of skill** (broadly permitted, state-dependent) from
+  **games of chance / gambling** (broadly prohibited). **Casino slots/roulette-type
+  play is chance** → not a "skill game."
+- There is **no central online-casino license** for chance games. Gambling is a
+  **state subject**; most states **prohibit** online gambling for money; a few have
+  specific regimes (e.g., Sikkim/Nagaland for limited scope, Goa land-based).
+- **28% GST on "online money gaming"** applies on the full face value of deposits/
+  bets in many readings — a heavy tax even where play is allowed.
+- Recent central legislation has moved to **ban real-money online games** — the
+  direction of travel is *more* restrictive, not less.
+
+**Practical conclusion for India (subject to counsel):**
+1. **Domestically, real-money chance-based casino is not a viable licensed path.**
+2. The **compliant domestic path is social-casino** — C74 virtual coins, **no
+   cash-out on the platform** (which is exactly the chosen architecture). Even then,
+   *paid* coin purchase for chance play is legally ambiguous and the 28% GST
+   question must be cleared → confirm with an Indian gaming + tax lawyer before
+   selling coins.
+3. If real-money is required, it is realistically served **only via an offshore
+   licensed operator (Track B) that lawfully accepts the permitted markets and
+   GEO-BLOCKS India** — not by licensing casino-for-cash inside India.
+
+**Track-A evidence to turn Gate 2 green:** an Indian gaming counsel opinion on
+(a) whether the specific product may take real money in the specific state(s),
+(b) the GST treatment, (c) advertising/consumer rules. Most likely output: "not
+for real-money chance play → social-casino only, or offshore + geo-block."
+
+---
+
+## Track B — Offshore licensed route (non-India players)
+
+For serving markets *outside* India where online casino is licensable. You license
+in a **gaming jurisdiction**, then serve **only** its permitted territories and
+**geo-block everyone else** (prohibited markets typically include the US, India,
+and many others — the license defines the list).
+
+**Common jurisdictions (compare with counsel — indicative only):**
+
+| Jurisdiction | Reputation | Indicative cost¹ | Indicative time¹ | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **Curaçao (CGA, new 2024+ regime)** | Mid, improving | ~€25k–100k+/yr all-in | ~3–6 months | Popular entry point; new regime tightened substance/AML; local requirements rising |
+| **Anjouan / Comoros** | Low-mid | Low (tens of $k) | Fast (~1–2 months) | Cheapest/fastest; weakest reputation; PSP/bank acceptance limited |
+| **Malta (MGA)** | High | High (€100k+ setup + capital) | ~6–12 months | Tier-1 credibility; heavy substance, capital, audits; EU access |
+| **Isle of Man / Gibraltar** | High | High | ~6–12 months | Tier-1; strong banking/PSP acceptance; strict |
+| **Kahnawake** | Mid | Mid | ~3–6 months | Established; N. America-adjacent nuance |
+
+¹ *Indicative ranges only — real figures depend on product, volume, structure, and
+change frequently. A licensed advisor must quote your case.*
+
+**Every offshore license requires (non-negotiable):**
+- Licensed **legal entity** in/acceptable to the jurisdiction (often local company + directors/substance).
+- **Share capital / financial requirements** per regime.
+- **Background / fit-and-proper checks** on owners/directors (UBO disclosure).
+- **AML/KYC program** (real identity verification — *not* auto-approve), **sanctions/PEP screening**, Travel-Rule.
+- **Responsible-gaming** controls (limits, self-exclusion — already built) + policy sign-off.
+- **RNG / game-fairness certification** by an accredited test lab (you have provably-fair server logic → get it formally certified).
+- **Geo-blocking** of all non-permitted markets, matching the license.
+- **Data protection** + player-funds segregation per the regime.
+- A **PSP that serves licensed gaming** under MCC 7995, tied to the license (Gate 3).
+
+---
+
+## Cross-cutting requirements (either track, before Gate 2 is green)
+
+1. **Entity & structure** — the operating company that will hold the license (Gate 1 partly done: a US LLC exists, but a US LLC is **not** a gaming licensee and carries higher US exposure; the licensed entity is usually formed in/for the chosen jurisdiction).
+2. **AML/KYC program** — documented, with real verification (turn OFF `kyc_auto_approve`; no-doc auto-approve is disqualifying).
+3. **Responsible gaming** — product built; needs policy sign-off.
+4. **Fairness certification** — accredited lab cert of the RNG/engine.
+5. **Geo-blocking** — enforced to match the license territories.
+6. **PSP approval** — gaming-approved processor for money-in (Gate 3).
+7. **Treasury** — funded, segregated, ≥100% liabilities (Gate 4).
+
+---
+
+## Phased plan
+
+| Phase | Action | Output / evidence | Gate |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| **L0** | Engage a **specialist gaming/regulatory attorney** + decide **target market(s)** | Market decision + written legal path | — |
+| **L1** | Counsel opinion: India (Track A) vs offshore (Track B); product classification; tax (GST) | Opinion memo → likely "social-casino domestic / offshore + geo-block for real-money" | Gate 2 scoping |
+| **L2** | If offshore: choose jurisdiction; form/adapt the **licensed entity**; UBO/fit-and-proper prep | Entity docs, jurisdiction chosen | Gate 1/2 |
+| **L3** | Build the compliance stack: AML/KYC program, RG policy sign-off, **fairness certification**, geo-block config | Program docs + lab cert + geo policy | Gate 5 |
+| **L4** | Submit license application; respond to regulator | **License certificate** (entity · products · territories) | **Gate 2 GREEN** |
+| **L5** | Gaming-approved **PSP** onboarding tied to the license | Written PSP gaming approval | **Gate 3 GREEN** |
+| **L6** | **Treasury** funding + segregation + on-chain verification | Custody ≥ obligations proof | **Gate 4 GREEN** |
+| **L7** | (If cash-out is offered) execute the **third-party provider** DD (`THIRD-PARTY-CASHOUT-DUE-DILIGENCE-CHECKLIST.md`) | Provider verified, contracted, opined | boundary §9 |
+| **L8** | Re-run the **8-system re-audit** → 8/8 GREEN | Register §10 stamp: GREEN | technical |
+| **L9** | Dual-control change window → supervised activation | `ENABLE REAL MONEY` (reserve invariant last guard) | GO-LIVE |
+
+---
+
+## What "Gate 2 GREEN" actually requires (evidence intake)
+A **valid license certificate** naming **your entity**, the **permitted products**
+(casino/slots/etc.), and the **permitted territories** — **plus** a geo-blocking
+policy that matches it. Nothing self-certified.
+
+**Hard stops:** no license · license doesn't cover your product · you'd be serving
+players outside the licensed territory (e.g., India/US when not permitted). Any of
+these ⇒ do not proceed.
+
+---
+
+## Honest summary
+- **India real-money chance casino:** realistically **not licensable domestically**;
+  compliant domestic path = **social-casino / no cash-out** (already the architecture);
+  real-money = **offshore license + geo-block India**, per counsel.
+- **Offshore route:** pick jurisdiction by reputation vs cost/time; expect months +
+  real capital + a full AML/RG/fairness/geo stack; the license then unlocks Gates 3–4.
+- **First action = engage counsel + choose the market.** Everything else follows.
+
+*Not legal advice. Figures are indicative and change; verify all specifics with a
+licensed gaming/regulatory + tax attorney in the target market before spending or
+committing. Nothing here is applied; `real_money_enabled` OFF.*
