+# AML / KYC Program Specification
+
+**Status:** compliance program design · **documentation only** · **Not legal advice.**
+**Companion to:** `EXTERNAL-GATES-CHECKLIST.md` (Gate 5), `LICENSE-ROADMAP.md`,
+`docs/audits/2026-08-22-systems-3-4-6-deep-dive.md` (#6), the consolidated register.
+
+> 🔒 **Scope guard.** Nothing here is applied. No production change, no migration,
+> no deploy, no flag flipped. `real_money_enabled` stays **OFF**. This specifies the
+> real AML/KYC program that must exist (and be sign-off'd by a compliance/AML
+> specialist under the license) before any real-money operation — and the code/
+> config changes it implies, all as **change-window** items.
+
+---
+
+## 0. Current state (audit evidence — must change)
+
+- `platform_settings.kyc_auto_approve = **true**`.
+- `kyc_prescreen` trigger **auto-approves** a submission to `status='approved'` when
+  it is enabled and **zero flags** are raised — and the **only** flags are
+  under-18/invalid-DOB and possible-duplicate-identity. **No document, ID, liveness,
+  address, or sanctions check.**
+- Evidence: `kyc_submissions` = **4 total → 4 approved → all 4 AUTO-APPROVED**.
+- The withdrawal AML gate (`request_crypto_withdrawal` requires an `approved` KYC row)
+  is therefore satisfiable by **self-declared** 18+ unique data.
+
+**Disqualifying for real money.** A real program must verify identity with evidence
+and never auto-approve identity on self-assertion.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Principles
+
+1. **Risk-based** — CDD by default, **EDD** for higher-risk (high value, PEP, high-risk geo, anomalous behaviour).
+2. **Real verification** — identity proven by **document + liveness**, not self-declaration.
+3. **No auto-approval of identity** — automation may **flag/pre-screen**, but a **human reviewer** (or an accredited IDV provider's verified result) sets `approved`.
+4. **Screen everyone** — sanctions/PEP at onboarding + ongoing.
+5. **Monitor continuously** — transaction monitoring, source-of-funds, re-screening.
+6. **Record & report** — retain evidence; file SAR/STR to the FIU when required.
+7. **Segregate duties** — MLRO/Compliance Officer owns approvals & reporting.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Program components
+
+### 2.1 Customer onboarding / CDD
+| Item | Requirement |
+|---|---|
+| Identity data | Legal name, DOB (**18+ hard gate**), nationality, residential address |
+| Government ID | Passport / national ID / driving licence — **document authenticity check** (via accredited IDV provider) |
+| Liveness / biometric | Selfie + liveness match to the ID (anti-spoof) |
+| Address proof | Utility bill / bank statement for higher tiers or where required |
+| Result | `verified` only after IDV pass **or** human review; else `pending`/`rejected` — **never** auto `approved` on self-data |
+
+### 2.2 Verification tiers (risk-based)
+| Tier | Trigger | Checks |
+|---|---|---|
+| **T1 Standard** | Default | ID + liveness + sanctions/PEP |
+| **T2 EDD** | High value / PEP / high-risk geo / anomaly | + source-of-funds/wealth, enhanced screening, senior sign-off |
+| **Blocked** | Under-18, sanctioned, prohibited geo, unresolved duplicate | Reject + record |
+
+### 2.3 Sanctions / PEP screening
+- Screen name/DOB against **sanctions + PEP + adverse-media** lists at onboarding.
+- **Ongoing re-screening** (list updates) + on material profile change.
+- Positive/possible match → hold + manual adjudication (never auto-clear).
+
+### 2.4 Ongoing / transaction monitoring
+- Rules: velocity, structuring/smurfing, rapid deposit→withdraw, mismatched geo/IP, dormant-then-large, chargeback patterns.
+- **Source-of-funds / source-of-wealth** requests over thresholds.
+- Alerts → case management → disposition (clear / EDD / SAR).
+
+### 2.5 Travel-Rule (crypto withdrawals)
+- For crypto transfers ≥ the applicable threshold, capture/transmit originator +
+  beneficiary information per the Travel-Rule; retain records.
+- Integrates with the **third-party cash-out** boundary — the party moving real
+  money owns Travel-Rule compliance (see boundary/DD docs).
+
+### 2.6 Record-keeping & retention
+- Retain identity evidence, screening results, monitoring alerts, and decisions for
+  the retention period required by the licensing jurisdiction (commonly 5+ years).
+- Immutable audit trail of who approved what and when.
+
+### 2.7 Suspicious Activity Reporting
+- Documented SAR/STR process to the relevant **FIU**; internal escalation to the
+  **MLRO**; no tipping-off; defined timelines.
+
+### 2.8 Governance
+- Named **MLRO / Compliance Officer**; documented policies; **staff training**;
+  **independent audit** of the program; board oversight.
+
+### 2.9 Responsible-gaming linkage
+- Deposit/loss limits + self-exclusion already built — connect to onboarding + monitoring; honour self-exclusion across the account lifecycle.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Required code / config changes (change-window items — NOT applied)
+
+| Change | Detail | Status |
+|---|---|---|
+| `kyc_auto_approve → false` | In the inbound-OFF change-set; identity no longer auto-approves | staged (change-set §2.2) |
+| `kyc_prescreen` **must never set `approved`** | Redesign: the trigger may only **flag/prescreen**; approval requires IDV-verified result or human reviewer. (New draft migration when the program is signed off.) | ⬜ to draft |
+| `withdrawal_auto_approve → false` | Restore human review on cash-out | staged (change-set §2.2) |
+| Real IDV integration | Accredited IDV/liveness provider; store `verification_status`, document refs, screening results | ⬜ design |
+| Sanctions/PEP screening | Provider integration + ongoing re-screen job | ⬜ design |
+| Transaction-monitoring rules | Rule engine + case management + SAR workflow | ⬜ design |
+| Data model | `kyc_submissions` extended (doc refs, IDV result, screening result, tier, reviewer, decision log); secure document storage with strict RLS | ⬜ design |
+
+> The two flag flips are already in `supabase/change-sets/2026-08-22-inbound-off.sql`.
+> The `kyc_prescreen` redesign + IDV/screening/monitoring integrations are new work
+> to be drafted **after** a compliance specialist signs off this program and the
+> licensing jurisdiction's exact rules are known.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Gate mapping
+
+- **Gate 5 (compliance)** GREEN when: this program is **documented, resourced
+  (MLRO), and signed off**; IDV + screening + monitoring are **live**; auto-approve
+  is **OFF**; SAR/retention processes exist; RG sign-off done; geo-block matches the
+  license.
+- Prereq: **Gate 2 license** (the jurisdiction defines the exact thresholds/rules).
+
+---
+
+## 5. What to do next
+1. **Engage a compliance/AML specialist** for the chosen licensing jurisdiction —
+   they define exact thresholds, list obligations, retention, and SAR routing.
+2. Select an **accredited IDV + screening provider**.
+3. Then draft the `kyc_prescreen` redesign + data-model migrations (branch-only) to
+   match the signed-off program.
+4. Keep `kyc_auto_approve`/`withdrawal_auto_approve` **OFF** from the change window on.
+
+*Not legal advice. AML/KYC obligations are jurisdiction-specific and must be defined
+and signed off by a qualified compliance/AML specialist under the license. Nothing
+here is applied; `real_money_enabled` OFF.*
-- 
