+# Incident note — "Importing a module script failed" (c7winners.com)
+
+**Date:** 2026-08-23 · **Surface:** iOS Safari on production (c7winners.com)
+**Status:** diagnosis + branch-only hardening. **No deploy performed here.**
+
+> 🔒 Scope: this documents a production *frontend* incident and a defensive
+> `vercel.json` change committed to `claude/checj-s0v7tw` only. Nothing deployed.
+> No backend/logic/money change. `real_money_enabled` remains OFF.
+
+## Symptom
+Branded error boundary (`src/ErrorBoundary.tsx`) shows **"C7 WINNERS ERROR —
+Importing a module script failed. undefined"** with a Reload button.
+
+## Root cause (mechanism)
+1. `src/main.tsx:21-52` already self-heals stale-client chunk errors: on a chunk
+   import failure it unregisters the service worker, clears caches, and hard-reloads
+   **once** (sessionStorage-guarded against loops). Seeing the error screen means the
+   self-heal **already fired**, reloaded, and the **fresh** page still failed → the
+   failure is **server-side**, not client cache.
+2. The served `index.html` module entry did not resolve to a real built chunk. The
+   SPA rewrite `"/(.*)" → "/index.html"` then returns **HTML (200, text/html)** for
+   the missing script path. iOS Safari importing HTML as a module reports exactly
+   **"Importing a module script failed."**
+3. Net: a **bad/partial production deploy** (failed `bun run build`, or a hashed
+   chunk missing on the CDN) served an `index.html` whose entry 404s → rewritten to
+   HTML → module import throws.
+
+## Immediate remediation (ops — not code)
+- **Vercel → Deployments → last healthy deploy → Instant Rollback.** Restores the
+  site immediately.
+- Or **redeploy the production commit with build cache cleared**, after confirming
+  `bun run build` succeeded and emitted `dist/assets/*.js` in the build logs.
+
+## Defensive hardening (this branch)
+`vercel.json` rewrite changed so **missing assets return a real 404** instead of
+HTML — which the existing self-heal handles cleanly, and which stops the confusing
+"HTML served as a module" failure mode:
+
+```
+- { "source": "/(.*)",                 "destination": "/index.html" }
++ { "source": "/((?!assets/|src/).*)", "destination": "/index.html" }
+```
+
+- Existing static files are unaffected (Vercel serves real files before rewrites).
+- A **non-existent** `/assets/index-<oldhash>.js` now 404s → the browser's chunk-error
+  self-heal reloads to the fresh graph, instead of importing an HTML fallback.
+- `/src/*` is also excluded so a stray dev-entry reference 404s loudly instead of
+  masquerading as HTML.
+
+**This is presentation/deploy-config only. It does not fix a broken build by itself —
+the broken deploy must still be rolled back or rebuilt.** It makes the failure mode
+fail safe and lets the self-heal work.
+
+*Branch-only. Not deployed. No backend/money change. `real_money_enabled` OFF.*
diff --git a/vercel.json b/vercel.json
index 1125036..c6e7fa3 100644
--- a/vercel.json
+++ b/vercel.json
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
   "outputDirectory": "dist",
   "framework": null,
   "rewrites": [
-    { "source": "/(.*)", "destination": "/index.html" }
+    { "source": "/((?!assets/|src/).*)", "destination": "/index.html" }
   ],
   "headers": [
     {
-- 
