+# Phase-0 · System-02 (Money Flow) — razorpay-webhook test evidence
+
+**Date:** 2026-08-23 · **Scope:** read-only audit + isolated local test · **documentation only**
+**Companion to:** `docs/audits/2026-08-22-consolidated-readiness-register.md`,
+`supabase/functions/razorpay-webhook/index.ts`,
+`supabase/tests/razorpay-webhook.local-test.mjs`
+
+> 🔒 **Scope guard.** No production change, migration, deploy, or flag flip. No edge
+> function deployed to production. `real_money_enabled` stays **OFF**. This records test
+> evidence for the inbound Razorpay deposit path; it does not enable any money rail.
+
+---
+
+## 0. What was tested and where
+
+| Layer | Method | Environment | Touches production? |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Signature / auth core | executed unit test (Node, exact function logic) | this audit sandbox | **No** |
+| Full deposit-credit flow | harness written + guard-tested; **not executed** here | needs local Docker stack / Pro branch | **No** |
+
+The isolated Supabase **branch** route was attempted and is **plan-blocked** (Supabase
+free plan: *"Branching is supported only on the Pro plan or above"*) — **no branch was
+created, $0 billed.** `supabase start` (local stack) needs a running Docker daemon, which
+the audit sandbox does not provide, so the full-flow harness runs on a Docker-capable
+machine (steps in §4).
+
+---
+
+## 1. Function under test
+
+`supabase/functions/razorpay-webhook/index.ts` — Razorpay calls it on payment events.
+Security model (from the source):
+
+- **Auth = HMAC-SHA256** over the **raw** request body, hex-encoded, keyed with
+  `RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (or the `gateway_secrets` store), constant-time compared to
+  the `x-razorpay-signature` header. `verify_jwt = false` (Razorpay sends no Supabase JWT).
+- **Amount is authoritative from the DB**, never the payload: it credits
+  `deposit_requests.amount` for the row correlated by `reference == order_id` (fallback:
+  `notes.deposit_id`), not any amount in the webhook body.
+- **Idempotent** credit via `apply_ledger_entry(p_idempotency_key='razorpay:<payment_id>')`
+  — Razorpay retry storms cannot double-credit.
+- Fail-safe correlation: DB errors return **500** (Razorpay retries) rather than a false
+  "ignored", so a genuinely-paid deposit is never silently dropped.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Executed evidence — signature / auth core (6/6 PASS)
+
+The function's `hmacSha256Hex` + `safeEqual` were run **verbatim** in Node against test
+vectors (harness: scratchpad `wh_test.mjs`).
+
+| # | Assertion | Result |
+|---|---|:--:|
+| 1 | Web-Crypto HMAC digest **==** Node `createHmac('sha256').digest('hex')` (Razorpay's documented algorithm) | ✅ PASS |
+| 2 | Valid signature **accepted** | ✅ PASS |
+| 3 | Tampered signature **rejected** | ✅ PASS |
+| 4 | Empty `x-razorpay-signature` header **rejected** (→ 401 path) | ✅ PASS |
+| 5 | Modified body → **different** signature (forgery/replay resistance) | ✅ PASS |
+| 6 | Length-mismatch short-circuits without crash | ✅ PASS |
+
+**Result: 6 passed, 0 failed.** Representative digest for the fixed test vector:
+`fc06aa7770c5fb1709c75639ae9d59ca9a3b3a5fae96ad2bc41a616aeacd094e`
+(test-only secret `whsec_test_ABC123`, not a real credential).
+
+**Conclusion:** the webhook's authentication boundary is correct — it computes the
+signature exactly as Razorpay specifies and accepts only genuine, untampered payloads.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Harness for the full deposit-credit flow (written, not yet executed)
+
+`supabase/tests/razorpay-webhook.local-test.mjs` — end-to-end against a local stack or
+isolated branch. Covers what §2 cannot without a running DB:
+
+| # | Scenario | Expected |
+|---|---|---|
+| A | HMAC-signed `payment.captured` for a seeded pending deposit | 200, wallet credited **exactly** `deposit.amount`, row → `credited` |
+| B | Replay the same webhook | 200, **no double-credit** (idempotent) |
+| C | Tampered signature | **401**, nothing credited |
+| D | Unknown order id | 200 ignored, nothing credited |
+
+**Guards verified in this session (exit 2 on each):**
+- Hard-refuses the production project ref `smcwrriaraptzjhqdktg`.
+- Refuses missing env, and non-local/non-branch hosts (unless `ALLOW_NONPROD_TARGET=1`).
+- Seeds a throwaway user + deposit row and tears them down; writes only to the target it is pointed at.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Run steps (Docker-capable machine)
+
+```bash
+supabase start
+supabase functions serve razorpay-webhook --no-verify-jwt --env-file supabase/.env.local
+
+SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321 \
+SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<local service_role key> \
+RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_local_test \
+node supabase/tests/razorpay-webhook.local-test.mjs
+```
+
+`RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET` must match what the served function reads. Capture the harness
+output (A–D pass/fail) + `supabase functions serve` logs and attach them under §3 to
+complete the System-02 inbound-deposit evidence.
+
+---
+
+## 5. System-02 status after this evidence
+
+| Item | State |
+|---|---|
+| Webhook signature/auth | ✅ **Verified** (6/6) |
+| Amount-from-DB (not payload) | ✅ confirmed by source review |
+| Idempotency design | ✅ confirmed by source review; ⏳ runtime proof pending §4 |
+| Full credit + double-credit runtime proof | ⏳ pending local/branch run (§4) |
+| Production posture | 🔒 unchanged — `real_money_enabled` OFF, no deploy |
+
+> Passing these tests validates the **mechanics** of the inbound path. It does **not**
+> move System-02 to GREEN for real money: that still requires the external gates
+> (license, gaming-approved PSP, funded treasury) and the dual-control change window per
+> the consolidated register. Nothing here authorizes go-live.
+
