diff --git a/docs/deploy/frontend-only.md b/docs/deploy/frontend-only.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b6cddbd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deploy/frontend-only.md
@@ -0,0 +1,153 @@
+# Frontend-only deploy kit
+
+**Purpose:** ship the C7 Winners SPA (presentation layer only) to a new host —
+Vercel or any static host — **without** activating any money layer. This is the
+safe path to publish the reskinned dashboard, login, and free-play surfaces.
+
+> **Scope guarantee.** This kit deploys **built static assets** (`dist/`) and
+> nothing else. It does **not** apply database migrations, deploy Supabase edge
+> functions, enable `real_money_enabled`, enable `IGAMING_ENABLED`, or touch any
+> deposit / withdrawal / crypto / ledger rail. Those systems stay exactly where
+> they are (OFF / interlocked). Deploying the frontend changes what users *see*,
+> not what the platform is *allowed to do* with money.
+
+---
+
+## What ships vs. what does NOT
+
+| Ships (safe, presentation) | Does NOT ship (money layer — stays off) |
+| --- | --- |
+| `dist/` static bundle (Vite build) | `supabase/migrations/**` (no `db push`) |
+| SPA routes (`/ig/*`, `/login`, `/play/*`) | `supabase/functions/**` (no `functions deploy`) |
+| Client reads via existing supabase-js (RLS-guarded) | `real_money_enabled` flag (stays OFF) |
+| C74 Originals **free-play** slots | `IGAMING_ENABLED` / 2J live launch (interlocked) |
+| Phone/Google auth UI (needs Twilio provider server-side) | Any deposit / payout / withdrawal / treasury rail |
+
+The SPA talks to the **same** Supabase project it always has, using the
+**anon/publishable** key and RLS. No new backend privilege is granted by a
+frontend deploy.
+
+---
+
+## Prerequisites (one-time, on the host)
+
+1. A Vercel project (or any static host) pointed at the new repo.
+2. Two **public, client-safe** env vars only:
+   - `VITE_SUPABASE_URL`
+   - `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` (a.k.a. publishable key)
+   These are the *only* secrets the frontend needs. They are already public by
+   design (they ship in the browser bundle and are protected by RLS).
+3. **Do NOT** add any of these to the host — they belong to the money layer and
+   have no place in a frontend-only deploy:
+   - `SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD`  ← would let CI run `db push`
+   - `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN` ← would let CI deploy edge functions
+   - `VERCEL_TOKEN` / `VERCEL_ORG_ID` / `VERCEL_PROJECT_ID` (for the *auto-promote*
+     workflow) ← would let a push to `main` promote to production automatically
+   - any PSP / crypto / treasury / service-role key
+
+---
+
+## Deploy config (already in repo)
+
+`vercel.json` at the repo root is already frontend-only and correct:
+
+- `buildCommand: "bun run build"` → Vite build
+- `outputDirectory: "dist"`
+- SPA rewrite: everything except `/assets/` and `/src/` → `/index.html`
+- long-cache headers for hashed assets, short-cache for `sw.js`
+
+No changes needed. If the new host uses npm instead of bun, set the build command
+to `npm run build` in the host UI (leave `vercel.json` as the source of truth
+where bun is available).
+
+---
+
+## In the NEW repo: disable the money-layer workflows
+
+The current `.github/workflows/` folder contains three workflows that fire on
+`push` to `main`. Each is **secret-gated** — it no-ops when its secret is absent —
+so they are already inert without the secrets above. For a frontend-only repo,
+**remove them entirely** so there is zero chance of accidental activation:
+
+- `deploy-migrations.yml`   (runs `supabase db push`)
+- `deploy-functions.yml`    (runs `supabase functions deploy`)
+- `deploy-production.yml`    (auto-promotes `main` → Vercel production)
+
+Keep only the safe CI:
+
+- `ci.yml`        (typecheck / test / build — keep)
+- `codeql.yml`     (static analysis — keep)
+- `preview.yml`     (PR preview build — keep if desired)
+- `deploy-pages.yml`  (GitHub Pages static — keep only if you want a Pages mirror)
+
+> Rule of thumb: if a workflow needs a `SUPABASE_*` or `VERCEL_TOKEN` secret to do
+> its job, it is **not** part of a frontend-only deploy. Delete it in the new repo.
+
+To remove them in the new repo:
+
+```bash
+git rm .github/workflows/deploy-migrations.yml \
+       .github/workflows/deploy-functions.yml \
+       .github/workflows/deploy-production.yml
+git commit -m "chore: frontend-only — drop money-layer deploy workflows"
+```
+
+Let Vercel's own **git integration** (connect repo in the Vercel dashboard) handle
+the static deploy on push. That path builds `dist/` and serves it — it never runs
+`supabase` anything.
+
+---
+
+## Local pre-flight gates (must be green before deploy)
+
+```bash
+npx tsc --noEmit      # types
+npx vitest run        # unit tests
+npx vite build        # production build → dist/
+```
+
+All three must pass. `vite build` producing `dist/` with no errors is the deploy
+artifact.
+
+---
+
+## Deploy steps (Vercel git-integration — recommended)
+
+1. In Vercel: **New Project → import the new repo**.
+2. Framework preset: **Other** (repo `vercel.json` drives build/output).
+3. Add env vars `VITE_SUPABASE_URL`, `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` (Production +
+   Preview). **Add nothing else.**
+4. Deploy. Vercel builds `dist/` and serves the SPA.
+5. (Optional) attach a domain. This does **not** point at `c7winners.com`
+   production unless you choose to — a fresh domain keeps the new deploy isolated
+   from any existing production.
+
+### Alternative: any static host
+
+`vite build` → upload `dist/` to Netlify / Cloudflare Pages / S3+CloudFront / GitHub
+Pages. Configure a **SPA fallback** to `index.html` (equivalent to the `vercel.json`
+rewrite) so client routes resolve. Set the two `VITE_*` vars at build time.
+
+---
+
+## Post-deploy verification
+
+- [ ] App loads; `/ig` dashboard renders.
+- [ ] `/login` shows phone-first + Google (codes only send if the Supabase Phone
+      provider/Twilio is enabled server-side — a frontend deploy cannot enable it).
+- [ ] Client-side reads work (profile, C74 summary) via anon key + RLS.
+- [ ] C74 Originals free-play (`/play/mayan-temple`) runs — **free-play, no money**.
+- [ ] 2J live-launch tiles remain interlocked (no real-money launch) — expected.
+- [ ] No deposit / withdraw rail is reachable — expected.
+
+---
+
+## Money-safety invariants (unchanged by this deploy)
+
+- `real_money_enabled` = **OFF**. A frontend deploy does not and cannot flip it.
+- `IGAMING_ENABLED` / 2J launch = **interlocked**. Unchanged.
+- No migration applied, no edge function deployed, no merge to `main` production.
+- The three money-layer workflows are removed (or remain secret-gated no-ops).
+
+This deploy is **presentation-only**. It is safe to publish because it grants no
+new money capability — it only serves the built UI.
-- 
