 ---
 
+## Connect the `c7winners.com` domain (frontend-only)
+
+Do this **after** the Vercel deploy is green and the post-deploy checklist passes —
+so the production domain only ever points at a build with the money surfaces OFF.
+
+1. In the Vercel project: **Settings → Domains → Add** → `c7winners.com`
+   (and `www.c7winners.com` if you want the www alias).
+2. Vercel shows the DNS records to set. At your domain registrar / DNS provider,
+   add them exactly as Vercel lists — typically:
+   - apex `c7winners.com` → **A record** to Vercel's anycast IP (Vercel shows the
+     current value, historically `76.76.21.21`), **or** an ALIAS/ANAME to
+     `cname.vercel-dns.com` if your DNS supports apex-CNAME.
+   - `www` → **CNAME** to `cname.vercel-dns.com`.
+   (Always copy the exact records from Vercel's Domains screen — they are the
+   source of truth and can change.)
+3. Wait for DNS to propagate; Vercel auto-issues the TLS certificate. The domain
+   goes **Valid** and `https://c7winners.com` serves the frontend build.
+4. Re-run the post-deploy checklist on the live domain — confirm **no deposit /
+   withdraw rail is reachable** and real-money surfaces stay OFF.
+
+**DNS and the Vercel dashboard are operator actions** — they need your registrar
+and Vercel access, so they can't be done from a coding session. The domain only
+serves what you deployed: a frontend-only build carries no money capability, so
+pointing `c7winners.com` at it is presentation-only.
+
+> Do **not** point the domain at a build that has `real_money_enabled` on, the
+> IGAMING launch un-interlocked, or deposit/withdraw enabled. Those require a
+> verified licence, an approved regulated PSP, and a funded, solvent reserve first.
+
+---
