+# Deploy the Catalog app to c7winners.com (Vercel)
+
+The React catalog app (this repo) becomes **c7winners.com**: it opens on the
+Instagram-style **reels frame** showing the activated 2J catalog. Presentation
+only — game launch stays **interlocked (501)**, no real-money surface.
+
+> The site currently deployed at c7winners.com is the separate **"C7 Chip Room"**
+> (the `c7winners` repo, `web/` folder). Moving the domain (step 5) is what
+> switches c7winners.com over to this catalog app. Keep the Chip Room by leaving
+> it on its own URL (e.g. `chips.c7winners.com`).
+
+---
+
+## 1. Get the code into a GitHub repo you own
+
+In your local clone of the **frontend** repo (the one Vercel will deploy):
+
+```bash
+git checkout -B main
+git am -3 c7-commits.mbox      # applies the 136 commits from this session
+git push -u origin main
+```
+
+If you don't have a repo yet, create an empty one on GitHub and push to it.
+
+## 2. Import the repo into Vercel
+
+- Vercel → **Add New… → Project** → import that repo.
+- Vercel auto-detects **`vercel.json`** already in the repo — do not override it:
+  - Build command: `bun run build`
+  - Output directory: `dist`
+  - Framework preset: Other (the repo pins `framework: null`)
+  - SPA rewrites for React Router are already configured.
+- If Vercel can't run `bun`, set **Build Command override** to `npm run build`
+  and **Install Command** to `npm install` in Project → Settings → General.
+
+## 3. Environment variables (Project → Settings → Environment Variables)
+
+Add for **Production** (and Preview):
+
+```
+VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://smcwrriaraptzjhqdktg.supabase.co
+VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_U-PDGrDaiMX5ldaVQeFldA_R7Yn3rKV
+VITE_PRESENTATION_ONLY=true
+```
+
+- These are **public** values (publishable key, RLS-protected). No secrets here.
+- `VITE_PRESENTATION_ONLY=true` keeps deposit/withdraw surfaces gated to demo.
+
+## 4. Deploy
+
+Trigger the first deployment (push, or the **Deploy** button). When it's green,
+open the `*.vercel.app` preview URL and confirm:
+
+- Opening `/` lands on the **reels frame** (65 activated 2J titles, real art).
+- A game tile → opens its detail; **Play** shows the interlocked / coming-soon
+  state (never a real-money launch).
+- No reachable deposit/withdraw money surface.
+
+## 5. Point c7winners.com at this project
+
+- In the **Chip Room** Vercel project → Settings → Domains → **remove**
+  `c7winners.com` (optionally re-add it there as `chips.c7winners.com`).
+- In **this** project → Settings → Domains → **Add** `c7winners.com`
+  (and `www.c7winners.com`). Follow Vercel's DNS instructions at your registrar
+  (A / CNAME) if the domain isn't already on Vercel.
+- Wait for DNS + SSL to go green.
+
+## 6. Verify on the live domain
+
+- `https://c7winners.com` → reels frame landing, real catalog, interlocked.
+- Hard-refresh a deep link (e.g. `/ig/explore`) — the SPA rewrite serves it
+  (no 404), confirming `vercel.json` is active.
+
+---
+
+## Setting the exact activated list (optional)
+
+The catalog defaults to the bundled 65 titles in `src/config/activeGames.json`.
+To override without a rebuild, set the `active_game_uids` key in Supabase
+`site_config` (JSON array of ids or `{uid,name,category}` objects) — the app
+reads it on load and shows exactly those, in that order. See
+`scripts/set-active-73.sql` for the shape.
+
+## Money-safety (unchanged)
+
+No real-money enablement here. `real_money_enabled` stays OFF, the `igaming`
+launch edge stays interlocked at 501, and C74 Originals remain free-play. This
+deploy is presentation only.
